1
00:00:13,013 --> 00:00:17,517
THE FIRST QUEST OF THE DESCEND CLUB

2
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:21,646
WATCH THE SUNRISE FROM TAEBAEKSAN

3
00:00:21,730 --> 00:00:26,067
SUNRISE EXPECTED AT 7:37 A.M.

4
00:00:26,151 --> 00:00:28,987
CURRENT LOCATION
YUILSA SHELTER

5
00:00:29,070 --> 00:00:31,740
52 MINUTES LEFT UNTIL THE SUN RISES

6
00:00:31,823 --> 00:00:34,868
One remaining 30-minute section
is as difficult as the beginning was.

7
00:00:34,951 --> 00:00:37,704
Think of it as 30 difficult minutes
and 30 easy minutes.

8
00:00:37,787 --> 00:00:38,621
-Okay.
-All right.

9
00:00:38,705 --> 00:00:39,539
Let's go quickly.

10
00:00:39,622 --> 00:00:40,915
Let's go while we're still fine.

11
00:00:40,999 --> 00:00:42,125
It's rising.

12
00:00:42,625 --> 00:00:43,835
It's coming up.

13
00:00:43,918 --> 00:00:47,255
LEAVING THE YUILSA SHELTER

14
00:00:47,338 --> 00:00:52,552
THEY'RE TAKING LONGER THAN EXPECTED
ON THE TRAIL

15
00:00:54,429 --> 00:01:01,394
THE STEEP SECTION STARTS IMMEDIATELY

16
00:01:08,359 --> 00:01:11,321
Well, this is nothing
compared to Seoraksan.

17
00:01:11,404 --> 00:01:12,947
My thoughts exactly.

18
00:01:13,740 --> 00:01:17,327
THE YOUNGER MEMBERS WITH GOOD STAMINA

19
00:01:18,495 --> 00:01:23,249
CAR, THE GARDEN TAKES LEAD

20
00:01:23,833 --> 00:01:29,339
THE FIRST STAIRCASE OF THIS TRAIL APPEARS

21
00:01:29,422 --> 00:01:33,259
CAR, THE FAST WALKER SPEEDS UP

22
00:01:33,343 --> 00:01:36,721
THEY HURRIEDLY MOVE PAST THE STAIRS

23
00:01:36,805 --> 00:01:39,933
NEXT IS THE STONE STAIRCASE SECTION

24
00:01:40,016 --> 00:01:45,688
CAR, THE GARDEN
FROM DOWOON'S CAM

25
00:01:46,356 --> 00:01:47,190
SIGHS

26
00:01:48,983 --> 00:01:49,943
I'm beat.

27
00:01:50,026 --> 00:01:51,277
It's okay. Take it slow.

28
00:01:51,778 --> 00:01:52,612
What?

29
00:01:52,695 --> 00:01:54,239
You can walk. Take it slow. It's fine.

30
00:01:54,322 --> 00:01:55,573
I'm walking very slowly.

31
00:01:55,657 --> 00:01:56,783
Really? That's good.

32
00:01:57,909 --> 00:01:59,828
Oh, no. It's getting brighter.

33
00:01:59,911 --> 00:02:01,371
It's okay. That's the light of dawn.

34
00:02:03,998 --> 00:02:05,625
We got up at 2:00 a.m. for this.

35
00:02:07,085 --> 00:02:08,962
-We have to see it.
-Yeah, we must.

36
00:02:09,045 --> 00:02:11,214
I think it'd feel so unfair if we miss it.

37
00:02:11,297 --> 00:02:12,549
Exactly. I'll get angry.

38
00:02:13,508 --> 00:02:14,425
We have to see it.

39
00:02:15,468 --> 00:02:17,095
I seriously thought, "If we fail,

40
00:02:17,595 --> 00:02:18,680
it'll be so disappointing."

41
00:02:18,763 --> 00:02:21,516
I mean, we even sacrificed sleep for this.

42
00:02:21,599 --> 00:02:24,435
"We have to pull this off."
That's what I was thinking.

43
00:02:31,776 --> 00:02:32,610
SIGHS

44
00:02:33,903 --> 00:02:35,905
<i>I must've strained it somehow.</i>

45
00:02:35,989 --> 00:02:39,409
Halfway through, this part here

46
00:02:39,492 --> 00:02:40,910
started to hurt.

47
00:02:41,619 --> 00:02:43,371
It's annoying when your leg hurts.

48
00:02:43,454 --> 00:02:45,165
And you have a mountain to climb.

49
00:02:45,248 --> 00:02:47,709
It's like eating with an injured finger.
It's annoying.

50
00:02:48,293 --> 00:02:49,127
That's how it felt.

51
00:02:49,210 --> 00:02:50,795
FATIGUED FROM HIKING IN TWO DAYS

52
00:02:51,880 --> 00:02:53,006
This is bullshit.

53
00:02:54,215 --> 00:02:55,133
Absolute bullshit.

54
00:02:55,216 --> 00:02:57,468
SUDDEN AND UNEXPECTED LEG PAIN

55
00:02:57,552 --> 00:02:59,095
I give up.

56
00:02:59,178 --> 00:03:04,267
GOING THROUGH
A DIFFICULT FIGHT WITH HIMSELF

57
00:03:04,350 --> 00:03:08,980
CAR, THE GARDEN
FROM DOWOON'S CAM

58
00:03:09,063 --> 00:03:11,649
Should we stop here
for just a bit of water?

59
00:03:12,150 --> 00:03:12,984
All right.

60
00:03:13,067 --> 00:03:14,694
-Sorry?
-Let's drink some water.

61
00:03:17,196 --> 00:03:18,031
Goodness.

62
00:03:18,865 --> 00:03:20,116
It sure is steep.

63
00:03:21,659 --> 00:03:25,371
A SHORT BREAK THANKS TO DOWOON

64
00:03:25,455 --> 00:03:26,873
Here you go.

65
00:03:26,956 --> 00:03:30,668
HELPER DOWOON PROVIDES A SPORTS DRINK

66
00:03:32,378 --> 00:03:33,796
-You can drink first.
-Thanks.

67
00:03:38,676 --> 00:03:39,677
I have water too.

68
00:03:44,432 --> 00:03:45,808
COLLECTS TRASH

69
00:03:45,892 --> 00:03:46,893
I feel hot already.

70
00:03:50,188 --> 00:03:51,022
SATISFIED SIGH

71
00:03:51,105 --> 00:03:53,358
LOOKING PROUDLY

72
00:03:53,441 --> 00:03:55,693
THEY CATCH A BREATHER
THANKS TO HELPER DOWOON

73
00:03:55,777 --> 00:03:57,320
I think we're almost there.

74
00:03:57,403 --> 00:03:58,488
-Let's go.
-Okay.

75
00:03:58,571 --> 00:03:59,739
Let's go.

76
00:04:01,324 --> 00:04:04,577
45 MINUTES BEFORE SUNRISE

77
00:04:05,787 --> 00:04:09,165
GETTING HIGHER AND HIGHER

78
00:04:10,041 --> 00:04:12,168
The sky is so pretty.

79
00:04:13,378 --> 00:04:14,629
Look at that gradient of color.

80
00:04:14,712 --> 00:04:15,755
Exactly.

81
00:04:17,257 --> 00:04:20,927
THE NATURAL GRADIENT OF COLOR
MADE BY THE LIGHT OF DAWN

82
00:04:22,679 --> 00:04:24,555
It sure is beautiful.

83
00:04:25,056 --> 00:04:27,767
Tarzzan should write
some rap lyrics inspired by that.

84
00:04:32,105 --> 00:04:33,648
It really is beautiful.

85
00:04:35,942 --> 00:04:37,318
The moon is up in the sky too.

86
00:04:38,903 --> 00:04:39,946
Look at the moon. Gosh.

87
00:04:41,030 --> 00:04:42,991
The sun on one side
and the moon on the other.

88
00:04:43,074 --> 00:04:44,075
Exactly.

89
00:04:53,584 --> 00:04:55,795
The moon and the sky look so beautiful.

90
00:04:57,839 --> 00:04:59,966
They're exactly the colors I like.

91
00:05:02,635 --> 00:05:03,886
The moon is so beautiful.

92
00:05:05,513 --> 00:05:09,767
<i>The moon was floating above the branches,</i>
<i>and it was just so…</i>

93
00:05:14,397 --> 00:05:15,773
<i>Violet?</i>

94
00:05:21,612 --> 00:05:24,282
<i>It reminded me of the movie</i>
The Twilight Saga: Eclipse.

95
00:05:26,451 --> 00:05:28,578
I wanted to take out my phone
to take a photo,

96
00:05:28,661 --> 00:05:30,121
but my hands were frozen.

97
00:05:30,204 --> 00:05:33,458
I just captured it with my eyes
and saved it to my brain.

98
00:05:38,212 --> 00:05:40,548
I thought,
"The GoPro must've captured it."

99
00:05:40,631 --> 00:05:41,674
Yeah, it was like that.

100
00:05:45,136 --> 00:05:46,179
It says 1.4 km.

101
00:05:47,722 --> 00:05:49,849
40 MINUTES BEFORE SUNRISE

102
00:05:49,932 --> 00:05:51,684
1.4 KM TO CHEONJEDAN ALTAR

103
00:05:52,685 --> 00:05:53,519
SIGHS

104
00:05:55,813 --> 00:05:59,859
THE PAIN REAPPEARS

105
00:06:01,778 --> 00:06:02,612
Goodness.

106
00:06:04,280 --> 00:06:05,698
-You can do this.
-Let's go.

107
00:06:05,782 --> 00:06:07,033
Take it slow. It's okay.

108
00:06:07,116 --> 00:06:08,618
-Okay.
-Take a break.

109
00:06:08,701 --> 00:06:11,120
We just need to run
100-m sprints 14 times, and it's over.

110
00:06:16,084 --> 00:06:23,049
HE BEGINS WALKING AGAIN

111
00:06:23,132 --> 00:06:29,347
STAIRS YET AGAIN

112
00:06:35,645 --> 00:06:37,105
AN AWKWARD SMILE

113
00:06:37,188 --> 00:06:38,523
-Should we rest?
-No, I can't.

114
00:06:38,606 --> 00:06:39,941
Let me rest for just 30 seconds.

115
00:06:40,024 --> 00:06:41,317
Okay. Let's wait.

116
00:06:43,069 --> 00:06:45,029
HIS BODY ISN'T LISTENING TO HIM

117
00:06:45,113 --> 00:06:46,239
More stairs had to show up.

118
00:06:46,948 --> 00:06:47,865
Goodness.

119
00:06:48,825 --> 00:06:49,826
How refreshing.

120
00:06:49,909 --> 00:06:50,952
Isn't this nice?

121
00:06:51,035 --> 00:06:52,120
I wanted to see your face.

122
00:06:52,829 --> 00:06:53,746
I missed you.

123
00:06:53,830 --> 00:06:55,206
TA-DA

124
00:06:55,289 --> 00:06:56,666
-You can go now.
-Let's go.

125
00:06:58,292 --> 00:06:59,210
We can do it.

126
00:07:01,671 --> 00:07:03,756
<i>His leg pain seemed to be</i>

127
00:07:04,257 --> 00:07:06,676
<i>a lot worse than I thought.</i>

128
00:07:06,759 --> 00:07:08,594
He kept checking on it.

129
00:07:08,678 --> 00:07:11,305
But he didn't panic at the pain.

130
00:07:11,389 --> 00:07:12,974
I would've panicked.

131
00:07:13,057 --> 00:07:15,017
Even in that condition,

132
00:07:15,101 --> 00:07:17,311
he quietly did what he had to do.

133
00:07:18,104 --> 00:07:20,314
It's only meaningful
if we all go together.

134
00:07:20,940 --> 00:07:22,358
So we went at the same pace.

135
00:07:23,568 --> 00:07:26,612
DESCEND CLUB MEMBERS
HIKE AT THE SAME PACE

136
00:07:26,696 --> 00:07:28,573
We're almost there. Hang in there.

137
00:07:29,824 --> 00:07:31,033
We're almost there.

138
00:07:34,328 --> 00:07:35,997
PAUSES

139
00:07:36,080 --> 00:07:38,833
THE SNOW IS STILL PILED UP HERE

140
00:07:39,417 --> 00:07:40,543
The trail…

141
00:07:41,377 --> 00:07:42,795
Is this really a trail?

142
00:07:42,879 --> 00:07:44,630
We're literally making a path.

143
00:07:45,673 --> 00:07:52,138
FROM EPISODE 3
YOU NEED TO RUSSELL THIS SECTION

144
00:07:53,598 --> 00:07:55,391
This is so beautiful.

145
00:07:55,475 --> 00:07:56,476
What's with this place?

146
00:07:59,395 --> 00:08:01,272
The stretched-out branches look so pretty.

147
00:08:01,355 --> 00:08:02,190
I know, right?

148
00:08:02,940 --> 00:08:05,067
It's something you'd see
in <i>Beauty and the Beast.</i>

149
00:08:07,695 --> 00:08:14,452
LIKE A SNOW TUNNEL FROM A FAIRY TALE

150
00:08:17,205 --> 00:08:21,083
THE SIGHT MAKES THEM FORGET
THE EXHAUSTION OF CLIMBING UPHILL

151
00:08:22,710 --> 00:08:25,505
I'm sorry to do this while you're tired,
but I'll explain one thing.

152
00:08:26,380 --> 00:08:27,465
Here.

153
00:08:27,548 --> 00:08:30,134
You really are persistent too.

154
00:08:31,677 --> 00:08:34,931
WE KNOW WE'RE PERSISTENT
BUT WE WANT TO SHOW YOU THIS SCENERY

155
00:08:35,014 --> 00:08:36,432
<i>This is called "rime."</i>

156
00:08:36,516 --> 00:08:37,850
<i>Snow is piled up on the branches.</i>

157
00:08:37,934 --> 00:08:38,768
RIME

158
00:08:38,851 --> 00:08:41,145
WATER VAPOR FREEZES
ON BRANCHES IN SUB-ZERO TEMPERATURES

159
00:08:41,229 --> 00:08:42,480
AND LOOKS LIKE WHITE BLOSSOMS

160
00:08:43,814 --> 00:08:47,568
FLOWERS MADE OF SNOW
BLOOM ON WINTER TREES

161
00:08:48,236 --> 00:08:52,907
A BEAUTIFUL SCENE OF WHITE
FOUND IN THE SNOWY MOUNTAINS

162
00:08:52,990 --> 00:08:54,242
<i>This is a yew tree.</i>

163
00:08:54,325 --> 00:08:56,869
<i>They're said to last 1,000 years living</i>
<i>and 1,000 years dead.</i>

164
00:08:56,953 --> 00:08:57,995
YEW TREE

165
00:08:58,079 --> 00:09:00,289
IT LIVES IN ALTITUDES
ABOVE 700 M ABOVE SEA LEVEL

166
00:09:00,373 --> 00:09:01,499
THEY CAN BE VERY LONG-LIVED

167
00:09:01,582 --> 00:09:02,917
YEW TREES GROW WILD ON TAEBAEKSAN

168
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:03,834
<i>These are yew trees.</i>

169
00:09:03,918 --> 00:09:06,003
<i>This is Korea's biggest yew tree colony.</i>

170
00:09:06,087 --> 00:09:09,298
<i>So as you pass by, you can see</i>
<i>a lot of unusual-looking trees.</i>

171
00:09:25,690 --> 00:09:27,733
Is this show funded by the government?

172
00:09:27,817 --> 00:09:30,778
This is like those absurd ads
in <i>The Truman Show.</i>

173
00:09:30,861 --> 00:09:32,863
He says stuff like this out of nowhere.

174
00:09:32,947 --> 00:09:34,532
Did you watch <i>The Truman Show?</i>

175
00:09:34,615 --> 00:09:38,035
In the movie, the wife of the protagonist
suddenly and awkwardly

176
00:09:38,119 --> 00:09:40,246
starts to advertise things.

177
00:09:40,329 --> 00:09:43,082
What he does feels just like that.

178
00:09:43,165 --> 00:09:45,585
It's not the right time for it,

179
00:09:45,668 --> 00:09:47,712
but he goes, "So this is…"

180
00:09:47,795 --> 00:09:49,922
As if he's obligated to say it.

181
00:09:50,840 --> 00:09:52,633
I just had to explain this one.
Nothing else.

182
00:09:52,717 --> 00:09:53,759
Okay, the yew tree colony.

183
00:09:53,843 --> 00:09:54,969
-Yew tree colony.
-Let's go.

184
00:09:55,052 --> 00:09:56,304
Ew tree colony?

185
00:09:56,804 --> 00:09:58,097
Yew tree colony?

186
00:09:58,180 --> 00:09:59,223
Ye…

187
00:09:59,307 --> 00:10:00,933
-It was "ye" something.
-"Ye."

188
00:10:01,017 --> 00:10:01,851
Ye…

189
00:10:02,893 --> 00:10:03,728
Yet…

190
00:10:04,687 --> 00:10:05,771
Yet tree.

191
00:10:06,564 --> 00:10:07,857
Yen tree.

192
00:10:07,940 --> 00:10:08,899
Yep tree.

193
00:10:10,359 --> 00:10:11,819
Was it the yew tree?

194
00:10:11,902 --> 00:10:12,737
Right.

195
00:10:12,820 --> 00:10:16,240
I remember because I planted that tree
in Hongneung Forest.

196
00:10:16,324 --> 00:10:19,493
<i>I planted a yew tree once</i>
<i>for a YouTube video.</i>

197
00:10:19,577 --> 00:10:22,705
<i>"The tree I planted with My Day."</i>

198
00:10:22,788 --> 00:10:24,624
So there's a DAY6 tree.

199
00:10:24,707 --> 00:10:26,626
<i>"Long after we're gone,</i>

200
00:10:26,709 --> 00:10:28,961
this tree will still be here."

201
00:10:29,045 --> 00:10:31,339
That's what I thought when I planted it.

202
00:10:33,633 --> 00:10:34,634
26 MINUTES BEFORE SUNRISE

203
00:10:34,717 --> 00:10:35,635
Let's check the time.

204
00:10:35,718 --> 00:10:37,595
-What time is it?
-It's 7:11 a.m.

205
00:10:37,678 --> 00:10:38,512
-Eleven?
-Yes.

206
00:10:39,096 --> 00:10:42,058
Okay. In this case, if we're late

207
00:10:42,141 --> 00:10:44,769
about five minutes, it's not our fault.

208
00:10:45,728 --> 00:10:50,816
THEY HAVE ENOUGH TIME TO REACH THE SUMMIT

209
00:10:52,652 --> 00:10:53,903
The sun's going to rise soon.

210
00:10:54,403 --> 00:10:55,946
I can tell from how the sky looks.

211
00:10:56,030 --> 00:10:57,865
THE SKY BECOMES BRIGHTER

212
00:11:04,080 --> 00:11:04,914
This is…

213
00:11:04,997 --> 00:11:06,415
Sir, I…

214
00:11:06,499 --> 00:11:07,667
-Producer.
-Yes?

215
00:11:07,750 --> 00:11:09,543
-I need…
-A break?

216
00:11:09,627 --> 00:11:11,170
It's really bad.

217
00:11:11,253 --> 00:11:12,672
-Your legs?
-Here.

218
00:11:12,755 --> 00:11:14,382
-Really?
-It feels like they're tearing.

219
00:11:15,049 --> 00:11:17,385
I wanted to say it earlier,
but I thought we were close.

220
00:11:17,927 --> 00:11:20,805
When Jung-won said it was an emergency,

221
00:11:20,888 --> 00:11:23,015
I suddenly got scared too.

222
00:11:23,641 --> 00:11:24,558
Go on ahead first.

223
00:11:25,768 --> 00:11:28,020
No, I don't think resting is a good idea.

224
00:11:28,646 --> 00:11:30,147
I'll move to the back. Go ahead.

225
00:11:30,231 --> 00:11:31,148
To the back?

226
00:11:31,232 --> 00:11:33,192
Resting will only make us feel cold.
Let's go.

227
00:11:33,275 --> 00:11:34,819
-Okay.
-I'll go to the back.

228
00:11:34,902 --> 00:11:35,986
Then…

229
00:11:36,070 --> 00:11:37,780
You feel your thighs will cramp?

230
00:11:37,863 --> 00:11:38,823
They already are.

231
00:11:38,906 --> 00:11:40,241
The back of his leg is cramping.

232
00:11:40,324 --> 00:11:42,785
When he said, "Let's just go,"

233
00:11:42,868 --> 00:11:44,912
I thought he was really…

234
00:11:44,995 --> 00:11:45,830
He did this,

235
00:11:46,997 --> 00:11:48,582
and he kept walking.

236
00:11:49,542 --> 00:11:52,420
"He must want to clear this quest too."

237
00:11:52,503 --> 00:11:54,463
<i>I felt that from him.</i>

238
00:11:55,339 --> 00:11:56,841
You go ahead. Let's go.

239
00:11:57,341 --> 00:11:58,467
It's too cold to stay here.

240
00:11:58,551 --> 00:12:00,219
-We're almost there.
-Okay.

241
00:12:00,302 --> 00:12:01,720
DOWOON AND TARZZAN GO FIRST

242
00:12:01,804 --> 00:12:05,558
CAR, THE GARDEN AND CHAE-MIN FOLLOW SUIT

243
00:12:05,641 --> 00:12:12,606
DOWOON, TARZZAN

244
00:12:12,690 --> 00:12:17,528
CAR, THE GARDEN, CHAE-MIN

245
00:12:18,279 --> 00:12:22,241
TAKING EACH STEP WITH DIFFICULTY

246
00:12:25,202 --> 00:12:26,787
THE INSTRUCTOR WANTS TO APPLY FIRST AID

247
00:12:26,871 --> 00:12:28,706
Let's check Jung-won's leg
before we continue.

248
00:12:28,789 --> 00:12:30,166
It's okay.

249
00:12:31,125 --> 00:12:32,376
-Let's just go.
-Are you sure?

250
00:12:32,460 --> 00:12:33,878
Yes. Please, let's just go.

251
00:12:33,961 --> 00:12:35,129
-You can do it.
-Thanks.

252
00:12:36,338 --> 00:12:40,384
DOWOON AND TARZZAN SET OFF FIRST AGAIN

253
00:12:43,471 --> 00:12:45,473
CURRENT LOCATION

254
00:12:45,556 --> 00:12:47,725
SUMMIT

255
00:12:48,476 --> 00:12:51,312
CAR, THE GARDEN IS DEEP IN THOUGHT

256
00:12:54,064 --> 00:12:59,612
THEY START HIKING AGAIN

257
00:13:11,624 --> 00:13:12,875
Darn it.

258
00:13:22,134 --> 00:13:23,135
Damn it.

259
00:13:26,680 --> 00:13:27,598
My gosh.

260
00:13:30,768 --> 00:13:31,602
Seriously…

261
00:13:35,356 --> 00:13:36,732
-I…
-Yes?

262
00:13:36,815 --> 00:13:38,567
I really can't do this show. Seriously.

263
00:13:40,444 --> 00:13:41,779
-Car-the.
-Goodness.

264
00:13:41,862 --> 00:13:42,696
Car-the.

265
00:13:42,780 --> 00:13:44,198
I really can't do this show.

266
00:13:44,281 --> 00:13:46,200
MAKES A NEGATIVE COMMENT
HE'S HELD BACK ALL DAY

267
00:13:46,283 --> 00:13:47,660
Jung-won?

268
00:13:47,743 --> 00:13:48,577
Jung-won.

269
00:13:49,078 --> 00:13:49,995
-You know, right?
-Yes.

270
00:13:50,079 --> 00:13:50,913
NEGATIVE GARDEN

271
00:13:50,996 --> 00:13:53,040
-Can you do this show?
-Of course.

272
00:13:53,123 --> 00:13:54,166
POSITIVE GARDEN

273
00:13:56,252 --> 00:13:58,045
-It's beautiful.
-You're full of lies.

274
00:13:58,128 --> 00:13:59,630
Exactly. The mountain is beautiful.

275
00:13:59,713 --> 00:14:00,589
It's beautiful.

276
00:14:00,673 --> 00:14:02,132
Look behind you. It's so beautiful.

277
00:14:03,008 --> 00:14:05,511
<i>When you struggle physically,</i>
<i>you definitely become weak.</i>

278
00:14:05,594 --> 00:14:06,512
<i>You become vulnerable.</i>

279
00:14:08,430 --> 00:14:11,475
You start making a lot of excuses.

280
00:14:12,851 --> 00:14:15,604
When you're so tired,
you get mentally weak too.

281
00:14:15,688 --> 00:14:19,149
So I thought,
"Those who hang on to their senses

282
00:14:19,817 --> 00:14:21,986
even when they're exhausted
are truly amazing."

283
00:14:29,076 --> 00:14:30,160
-Let's wait for them.
-Yeah.

284
00:14:32,788 --> 00:14:34,957
<i>I felt anxious, but I thought I shouldn't.</i>

285
00:14:35,040 --> 00:14:37,793
<i>I thought Jung-won would feel pressured.</i>

286
00:14:38,294 --> 00:14:40,629
I'm sure he was thinking the same thing.

287
00:14:40,713 --> 00:14:42,381
"We can't slow down because of me."

288
00:14:42,464 --> 00:14:44,341
He must've thought that.

289
00:14:44,425 --> 00:14:45,426
I just…

290
00:14:46,343 --> 00:14:47,970
didn't want to pressure him.

291
00:14:48,053 --> 00:14:50,389
"What? That quest?"

292
00:14:50,890 --> 00:14:53,809
"Come on. As if the reward for it
will be that great."

293
00:14:53,893 --> 00:14:56,020
I wanted to express

294
00:14:56,103 --> 00:14:58,105
those feelings to him.

295
00:15:00,900 --> 00:15:01,942
We're almost there.

296
00:15:04,361 --> 00:15:05,404
We're here.

297
00:15:05,905 --> 00:15:07,114
The uphill part is over.

298
00:15:09,408 --> 00:15:10,242
Here…

299
00:15:11,493 --> 00:15:12,328
Let's just go.

300
00:15:13,078 --> 00:15:14,121
-It's cold.
-Okay.

301
00:15:19,209 --> 00:15:22,129
We have five minutes to go.
We'll arrive in five minutes.

302
00:15:22,212 --> 00:15:23,422
Nice.

303
00:15:24,506 --> 00:15:27,760
10 MINUTES BEFORE SUNRISE

304
00:15:35,225 --> 00:15:36,685
We're almost there.

305
00:15:36,769 --> 00:15:38,228
Would you like to take a break?

306
00:15:38,312 --> 00:15:39,480
Are you all right?

307
00:15:55,663 --> 00:15:58,916
6 MINUTES BEFORE SUNRISE

308
00:15:59,917 --> 00:16:00,876
What time is it?

309
00:16:02,211 --> 00:16:03,671
It's 7:31 a.m.

310
00:16:04,213 --> 00:16:05,214
The sun is slowly rising.

311
00:16:05,297 --> 00:16:07,424
It should fully rise
when we get to Janggunbong Peak.

312
00:16:08,801 --> 00:16:11,553
THE SUN PEEKS OUT SLIGHTLY

313
00:16:14,390 --> 00:16:15,307
We're really here.

314
00:16:17,685 --> 00:16:19,812
JANGGUNBONG IS JUST OVER THE HILL

315
00:16:20,521 --> 00:16:26,110
THEY MARCH TO THE HILL
WITH ALL THEIR REMAINING STRENGTH

316
00:16:26,193 --> 00:16:28,112
Isn't this a successful completion?

317
00:16:28,946 --> 00:16:29,905
ARRIVED AT JANGGUNBONG

318
00:16:29,989 --> 00:16:32,324
-What's the time?
-It's 7:33 a.m.

319
00:16:32,408 --> 00:16:33,242
That means…

320
00:16:33,325 --> 00:16:34,827
Seeing the sunrise on Taebaeksan.

321
00:16:34,910 --> 00:16:36,078
You've cleared the quest.

322
00:16:36,161 --> 00:16:39,123
THE FIRST QUEST IS COMPLETE

323
00:16:39,832 --> 00:16:41,041
Good job, Jung-won.

324
00:16:41,125 --> 00:16:41,959
Good job.

325
00:16:42,042 --> 00:16:43,335
-Good job.
-Well done.

326
00:16:43,419 --> 00:16:44,253
Good job, everyone.

327
00:16:57,141 --> 00:16:58,100
<i>When I saw the sunrise?</i>

328
00:16:58,183 --> 00:17:02,980
<i>We did have to rush our hike,</i>
<i>as if someone was chasing us.</i>

329
00:17:04,189 --> 00:17:05,232
But still,

330
00:17:05,899 --> 00:17:07,651
we saw the sun on the horizon.

331
00:17:08,152 --> 00:17:10,070
The sun rose just in time too.

332
00:17:10,154 --> 00:17:11,405
So, yeah…

333
00:17:12,322 --> 00:17:13,532
<i>It was really nice.</i>

334
00:17:13,615 --> 00:17:16,618
JANGGUNBONG

335
00:17:28,881 --> 00:17:30,007
<i>As soon as we got up there,</i>

336
00:17:30,507 --> 00:17:33,552
it was the summit,
and nothing else was higher than that.

337
00:17:33,635 --> 00:17:37,765
The open view was really beautiful.

338
00:17:58,035 --> 00:18:00,496
Actually, I wanted
to stay up there longer,

339
00:18:00,579 --> 00:18:02,581
but there was no suitable place to stay.

340
00:18:02,664 --> 00:18:06,085
The wind was blowing so hard.

341
00:18:06,668 --> 00:18:11,673
CURRENT WIND SPEED
"STRONG"

342
00:18:13,550 --> 00:18:14,384
My gloves!

343
00:18:14,468 --> 00:18:15,719
GLOVES FLY AWAY IN THE WIND

344
00:18:16,887 --> 00:18:18,639
My hands are frozen. I can't untie this.

345
00:18:21,225 --> 00:18:26,313
WEARING PADDED JACKETS
TO SHIELD AGAINST THE STRONG WIND

346
00:18:26,396 --> 00:18:28,816
It definitely was pretty windy.

347
00:18:28,899 --> 00:18:30,901
It was so cold up there.

348
00:18:31,485 --> 00:18:32,820
I was stunned.

349
00:18:32,903 --> 00:18:34,446
It was way too cold today.

350
00:18:36,240 --> 00:18:39,827
RUSTLING

351
00:18:40,786 --> 00:18:42,162
Jung-won, at least eat this.

352
00:18:42,246 --> 00:18:43,080
It's okay.

353
00:18:43,163 --> 00:18:44,081
You can't eat at all?

354
00:18:44,164 --> 00:18:44,998
No.

355
00:18:48,669 --> 00:18:49,586
What would you like?

356
00:18:49,670 --> 00:18:51,505
-Thank you, Dowoon.
-What do you want to eat?

357
00:18:51,588 --> 00:18:53,465
I'll go with the cocoa ball bar.

358
00:18:53,549 --> 00:18:55,467
HELPER DOWOON WORKS HARD AT THE SUMMIT TOO

359
00:18:55,551 --> 00:18:56,718
Why don't you have one?

360
00:18:58,345 --> 00:18:59,596
Is it harder to eat?

361
00:19:00,180 --> 00:19:01,265
I'll keep one, then.

362
00:19:01,348 --> 00:19:02,558
Thanks.

363
00:19:03,142 --> 00:19:03,976
Okay.

364
00:19:06,186 --> 00:19:07,771
Let's take a photo, everyone.

365
00:19:07,855 --> 00:19:08,689
Okay.

366
00:19:09,690 --> 00:19:14,069
LAST-MINUTE SUGAR BOOST
BEFORE TAKING PHOTOS

367
00:19:14,153 --> 00:19:17,072
DESCEND CLUB'S FIRST PHOTO
WITH A SUMMIT MARKER

368
00:19:18,532 --> 00:19:20,409
YUM

369
00:19:21,160 --> 00:19:23,871
TAKING A GROUP PHOTO IN THE BITING WIND

370
00:19:23,954 --> 00:19:26,165
GETTING CHOKED UP

371
00:19:26,248 --> 00:19:28,083
Here we go. One, two, three.

372
00:19:30,502 --> 00:19:34,464
JANUARY 14, 2026
SUNRISE AT JANGGUNBONG, TAEBAEKSAN

373
00:19:34,548 --> 00:19:36,216
Shall we strike a pose?

374
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:37,968
Like a peace sign or a fist pump?

375
00:19:38,051 --> 00:19:39,428
-Let's go!
-Let's go!

376
00:19:39,511 --> 00:19:40,888
One, two, three.

377
00:19:45,684 --> 00:19:47,394
I wanted to go down quickly.

378
00:19:49,104 --> 00:19:51,064
It was so cold. I just…

379
00:19:51,732 --> 00:19:53,066
Taking photos was so hard.

380
00:19:53,775 --> 00:19:55,611
You need to force yourself
to look excited.

381
00:19:56,486 --> 00:19:58,113
The face we wanted to make

382
00:19:59,156 --> 00:20:00,240
was that.

383
00:20:00,324 --> 00:20:02,534
-One more time.
-With a good view of the sun too.

384
00:20:05,537 --> 00:20:06,371
FAKE EXCITEMENT

385
00:20:06,455 --> 00:20:07,581
Put your hands up.

386
00:20:07,664 --> 00:20:09,666
Last photo. One, two, three.

387
00:20:11,335 --> 00:20:13,003
When we were taking the photos,

388
00:20:14,046 --> 00:20:15,297
I couldn't smile

389
00:20:16,089 --> 00:20:17,382
because it was so cold.

390
00:20:17,466 --> 00:20:20,177
<i>My cheeks had frozen.</i>

391
00:20:20,719 --> 00:20:21,845
<i>But…</i>

392
00:20:21,929 --> 00:20:25,349
<i>Dowoon gave out his energy bars,</i>

393
00:20:25,432 --> 00:20:27,142
<i>so I felt a bit better after eating it.</i>

394
00:20:29,895 --> 00:20:30,896
This is good.

395
00:20:30,979 --> 00:20:32,773
I told you. You need to eat.

396
00:20:32,856 --> 00:20:35,234
There's a reason we refuel with sugar.

397
00:20:36,276 --> 00:20:37,110
Thank you.

398
00:20:39,446 --> 00:20:40,614
Thanks for the energy bar.

399
00:20:40,697 --> 00:20:41,531
No problem.

400
00:20:41,615 --> 00:20:42,991
-Thank you.
-Sure.

401
00:20:45,869 --> 00:20:48,830
CHOMPING

402
00:20:49,414 --> 00:20:50,374
This tastes good.

403
00:20:50,916 --> 00:20:52,000
Eating this revived me.

404
00:20:52,793 --> 00:20:53,627
Do you want a bite?

405
00:20:53,710 --> 00:20:54,586
I'm good.

406
00:20:55,254 --> 00:20:57,339
But then again, food always comes first.

407
00:20:59,091 --> 00:21:01,760
CHOMPING AGAIN

408
00:21:01,843 --> 00:21:05,097
I remember the chocolate bar tasted good.

409
00:21:05,180 --> 00:21:06,181
Who gave it to you?

410
00:21:06,265 --> 00:21:07,266
Dowoon.

411
00:21:07,349 --> 00:21:08,684
He is today's MVP.

412
00:21:09,810 --> 00:21:10,852
TARZZAN'S TAEBAEKSAN MVP

413
00:21:10,936 --> 00:21:13,313
I felt good after giving those out.

414
00:21:13,814 --> 00:21:14,940
I felt good.

415
00:21:15,023 --> 00:21:17,985
When you hike, you crave sugar.

416
00:21:18,068 --> 00:21:19,611
You really crave sugar.

417
00:21:19,695 --> 00:21:21,613
When you take a bite of an energy bar,

418
00:21:22,197 --> 00:21:23,448
you think,

419
00:21:23,532 --> 00:21:27,035
"Did these always taste this good?"

420
00:21:28,745 --> 00:21:35,711
MEANWHILE, THE ONE WHO REFUSED TO EAT

421
00:21:36,753 --> 00:21:39,339
Jung-won declined once.

422
00:21:39,423 --> 00:21:41,425
"It's okay." He refused like this.

423
00:21:41,508 --> 00:21:43,218
I said, "You should still try it."

424
00:21:43,302 --> 00:21:45,887
I gave him one, and he really enjoyed it.

425
00:21:45,971 --> 00:21:48,682
That guy always refuses
to listen at first.

426
00:21:50,392 --> 00:21:52,227
CHECKING ON THAT GUY'S CONDITION

427
00:21:52,311 --> 00:21:53,353
Behind my knee.

428
00:21:53,437 --> 00:21:54,521
-Behind your knee?
-Here.

429
00:21:55,605 --> 00:21:57,441
Since we'll be going down,
it should be fine.

430
00:21:57,524 --> 00:21:58,358
I'll give it a try.

431
00:21:59,693 --> 00:22:03,238
YUM

432
00:22:03,322 --> 00:22:04,323
Let's go.

433
00:22:05,490 --> 00:22:08,076
THEY START TO DESCEND

434
00:22:08,160 --> 00:22:11,371
TAKING THE DANGGOL PLAZA TRAIL DOWNHILL

435
00:22:12,831 --> 00:22:14,166
Now, it's "good morning."

436
00:22:14,750 --> 00:22:15,584
Yeah.

437
00:22:16,543 --> 00:22:18,587
THE DESCENT BEGINS

438
00:22:18,670 --> 00:22:20,589
Once we're down,
some barbecue would be amazing.

439
00:22:22,632 --> 00:22:24,092
Gosh, Tarzzan.

440
00:22:24,176 --> 00:22:25,010
Yes?

441
00:22:25,093 --> 00:22:26,470
Going downhill is so easy.

442
00:22:26,553 --> 00:22:27,387
Right?

443
00:22:27,929 --> 00:22:28,764
My ankles…

444
00:22:29,806 --> 00:22:31,475
What a magnificent view.

445
00:22:32,559 --> 00:22:34,394
It sure is beautiful, though.

446
00:22:35,479 --> 00:22:37,606
It's spectacular.

447
00:22:38,231 --> 00:22:40,650
I'd never get to see
something like this again.

448
00:22:42,235 --> 00:22:44,529
The view on my right.

449
00:22:47,157 --> 00:22:51,620
WHERE THE MORNING SUN SHINES

450
00:22:51,703 --> 00:22:54,956
<i>The scenery around me felt quite flat.</i>

451
00:22:55,040 --> 00:22:56,374
That made it even more beautiful.

452
00:22:56,458 --> 00:22:59,127
I think I got to see
what a real snow mountain looks like.

453
00:23:20,732 --> 00:23:21,691
My hands are so cold.

454
00:23:28,865 --> 00:23:34,079
THEY ARRIVE AT THE CHEONJEDAN

455
00:23:34,162 --> 00:23:34,996
TAEBAEKSAN

456
00:23:35,080 --> 00:23:35,914
What does that say?

457
00:23:36,623 --> 00:23:38,416
I think that indicates the summit.

458
00:23:38,959 --> 00:23:40,877
So a lot of people take photos here.

459
00:23:42,170 --> 00:23:46,883
CHEONJEDAN, JANGGUNBONG

460
00:23:47,676 --> 00:23:51,763
ANOTHER POPULAR SPOT
FOR SEEING THE SUNRISE

461
00:23:52,597 --> 00:23:53,431
TAEBAEKSAN

462
00:23:53,515 --> 00:23:56,309
THE PLACE WHERE TAEBAEKSAN'S
STONE ALTAR IS LOCATED

463
00:24:00,814 --> 00:24:02,732
I'm on Taebaeksan, everyone.

464
00:24:04,943 --> 00:24:05,777
Taebaeksan.

465
00:24:05,861 --> 00:24:08,029
FIRST TIME PROVING HE'S AT THE SUMMIT

466
00:24:08,113 --> 00:24:12,742
YOU CAN CHECK ON CCTV AS WELL

467
00:24:13,451 --> 00:24:16,204
The mountains you see beyond mountains
are called <i>sangeurime.</i>

468
00:24:16,288 --> 00:24:17,122
"San?"

469
00:24:17,205 --> 00:24:19,166
<i>Sangeurime.</i> It's a pure Korean word.

470
00:24:19,249 --> 00:24:20,917
-"<i>Geurimhae</i>"?
-They look like shadows.

471
00:24:21,001 --> 00:24:22,961
SANGEURIME OR MOUNTAIN SILHOUETTE

472
00:24:23,044 --> 00:24:27,507
THE FAINT VIEW OF DISTANT MOUNTAINS
LINED UP IN LAYERS LIKE SHADOWS

473
00:24:40,520 --> 00:24:41,646
This is easy.

474
00:24:41,730 --> 00:24:42,939
THE DESCENT STARTS AGAIN

475
00:24:43,023 --> 00:24:45,442
Doesn't it feel like
an amusement park in the winter?

476
00:24:45,525 --> 00:24:47,068
-A winter amusement park?
-Yeah.

477
00:24:47,152 --> 00:24:49,112
-Why?
-If you go to Everland in the winter…

478
00:24:49,196 --> 00:24:50,071
Yeah?

479
00:24:50,155 --> 00:24:52,324
You can ride sleds and so on.

480
00:24:52,407 --> 00:24:55,118
But what good does that do?
We can't get on any sleds.

481
00:24:56,703 --> 00:24:58,788
I should bring a pack next time.

482
00:24:58,872 --> 00:25:00,707
What am I saying? I mean a sack.

483
00:25:00,790 --> 00:25:03,418
Yeah, I think we could ride it
as long as it's not Seoraksan.

484
00:25:03,501 --> 00:25:04,502
I know, right?

485
00:25:05,420 --> 00:25:06,671
I saw your Instagram yesterday.

486
00:25:06,755 --> 00:25:08,924
You were number one
on the Apple Music chart.

487
00:25:09,007 --> 00:25:10,300
Yes, number one on Apple Music.

488
00:25:10,383 --> 00:25:11,843
Congratulations.

489
00:25:11,927 --> 00:25:14,387
And 26th on Melon.
It's my first time ranking so high.

490
00:25:14,471 --> 00:25:15,388
Number 26 on Melon?

491
00:25:15,472 --> 00:25:16,306
Yes.

492
00:25:16,389 --> 00:25:17,474
ON THE DAY OF FILMING

493
00:25:17,557 --> 00:25:20,310
CAR, THE GARDEN'S SONG "MY WHOLE WORLD"
HAD A RESURGENCE

494
00:25:20,393 --> 00:25:21,603
AND TOPPED A MUSIC CHART

495
00:25:21,686 --> 00:25:22,771
TODAY'S TOP 100 IN KOREA

496
00:25:22,854 --> 00:25:24,231
-Congratulations.
-Thank you.

497
00:25:26,483 --> 00:25:28,652
In the end, the song
became a belated success.

498
00:25:28,735 --> 00:25:30,362
All sorts of things can happen in life.

499
00:25:31,488 --> 00:25:34,532
My fellow musicians call me
"the icon of toughing it out."

500
00:25:35,408 --> 00:25:37,160
Only now, I am…

501
00:25:37,994 --> 00:25:40,497
I'm a bit embarrassed to say
it's thanks to my music.

502
00:25:40,580 --> 00:25:42,958
I was able to catch people's attention

503
00:25:43,541 --> 00:25:45,126
with variety show-like content.

504
00:25:46,002 --> 00:25:48,505
I mean, any attention
is still good attention.

505
00:25:49,297 --> 00:25:51,174
But at the end of the day, I'm a musician.

506
00:25:51,841 --> 00:25:54,970
It's nice for my songs to get noticed.

507
00:25:55,053 --> 00:25:56,429
So I was working hard.

508
00:25:58,890 --> 00:26:00,850
-I got excited yesterday.
-Right.

509
00:26:00,934 --> 00:26:02,269
I should've slept at midnight.

510
00:26:02,978 --> 00:26:04,187
You posted on Instagram.

511
00:26:04,271 --> 00:26:05,480
People from my agency

512
00:26:06,231 --> 00:26:07,691
kept hyping me up.

513
00:26:08,275 --> 00:26:09,567
I couldn't sleep until 1:00 a.m.

514
00:26:11,319 --> 00:26:13,196
LAST NIGHT

515
00:26:13,280 --> 00:26:16,700
Jung-won, you're number one
on Apple Music in Korea.

516
00:26:16,783 --> 00:26:19,202
I'm with Korea's
number one singer right now.

517
00:26:19,286 --> 00:26:21,454
To be honest, I feel very happy today.

518
00:26:22,872 --> 00:26:25,000
This is my first time experiencing this.

519
00:26:33,133 --> 00:26:37,137
HUMMING

520
00:26:37,887 --> 00:26:39,431
But the thing is

521
00:26:40,015 --> 00:26:44,894
I always share song copyrights equally
with my bandmates who I love

522
00:26:44,978 --> 00:26:46,146
and always work with.

523
00:26:46,229 --> 00:26:48,231
I never consider who worked more on what.

524
00:26:48,315 --> 00:26:49,983
Because I never thought

525
00:26:50,066 --> 00:26:51,609
I'd ever chart that high.

526
00:26:52,694 --> 00:26:54,029
But as I was hiking, I thought,

527
00:26:54,112 --> 00:26:55,030
"Damn it."

528
00:26:57,115 --> 00:26:58,742
"Should I change the split?"

529
00:26:58,825 --> 00:27:00,493
"I think I worked more on this song."

530
00:27:00,577 --> 00:27:01,619
BLACK-HEARTED

531
00:27:01,703 --> 00:27:04,122
I'm such a poor excuse for a human being.

532
00:27:04,205 --> 00:27:06,750
I'm so low-quality as a person.

533
00:27:06,833 --> 00:27:08,752
You get what I mean?

534
00:27:09,336 --> 00:27:11,504
I'm so lame.

535
00:27:11,588 --> 00:27:14,841
"Jung-won, since you're exhausted,
you're being so lame."

536
00:27:14,924 --> 00:27:16,009
So lame.

537
00:27:16,092 --> 00:27:19,471
It's like whenever Gollum
is near the One Ring.

538
00:27:20,347 --> 00:27:21,514
You start acting like that.

539
00:27:24,934 --> 00:27:28,313
HAS A LOT ON HIS MIND

540
00:27:30,690 --> 00:27:33,693
At least the way down
is pretty smooth, right?

541
00:27:33,777 --> 00:27:34,611
Yeah.

542
00:27:35,278 --> 00:27:36,905
I like how there are no rocks.

543
00:27:36,988 --> 00:27:40,367
Yeah, and I can even look around.

544
00:27:40,450 --> 00:27:42,327
Exactly. I can look around today.

545
00:27:42,410 --> 00:27:43,244
Yeah.

546
00:27:47,082 --> 00:27:50,710
THE SNOWSCAPE SHINES BRIGHTER
IN THE MORNING SUN

547
00:28:06,017 --> 00:28:08,853
If Seoraksan had very exciting vibes,

548
00:28:08,937 --> 00:28:11,189
then this place had relaxed
and comforting vibes.

549
00:28:11,272 --> 00:28:12,315
Your body is cold,

550
00:28:12,399 --> 00:28:14,901
but your heart feels warm
while on the mountain.

551
00:28:14,984 --> 00:28:16,403
That's the energy it gives off.

552
00:28:32,919 --> 00:28:35,672
Rather than the sunrise itself,

553
00:28:36,923 --> 00:28:39,050
the snowy mountain scenery
was more beautiful.

554
00:28:41,469 --> 00:28:48,435
THEY ENJOY THE SNOWSCAPE
AS THEY DESCEND

555
00:28:52,480 --> 00:28:54,190
I like how the ground feels here.

556
00:28:56,818 --> 00:28:59,988
BANJAE PASS

557
00:29:05,410 --> 00:29:06,953
How far have we come?

558
00:29:07,036 --> 00:29:08,079
About one-third?

559
00:29:08,705 --> 00:29:09,789
You're halfway there.

560
00:29:11,624 --> 00:29:14,586
THEY TAKE A SHORT BREAK

561
00:29:14,669 --> 00:29:15,503
Want some candy?

562
00:29:17,255 --> 00:29:18,548
No, I'm good.

563
00:29:21,259 --> 00:29:22,343
Are your legs okay?

564
00:29:22,844 --> 00:29:23,678
No, they hurt.

565
00:29:25,013 --> 00:29:27,098
DEPRESSED

566
00:29:27,182 --> 00:29:29,058
-Do you want some caramel?
-Should I have one?

567
00:29:29,142 --> 00:29:30,185
Yeah, if you're hungry.

568
00:29:31,311 --> 00:29:33,855
YOON DORAEMON HAS
AN INFINITE SUPPLY OF TRAIL FOOD

569
00:29:37,108 --> 00:29:38,234
Go on ahead.

570
00:29:39,068 --> 00:29:40,987
We're opening caramels.
We'll be right there.

571
00:29:41,529 --> 00:29:42,572
Go ahead.

572
00:29:43,406 --> 00:29:45,033
The caramels have frozen.

573
00:29:45,116 --> 00:29:45,950
Right.

574
00:29:46,034 --> 00:29:48,286
Every time we descend like this,

575
00:29:48,912 --> 00:29:50,997
I realize that we climbed up a long way.

576
00:29:51,873 --> 00:29:53,875
I'm not going to think anymore.

577
00:29:54,918 --> 00:29:56,336
You shouldn't think.

578
00:29:57,086 --> 00:29:58,505
As you walk, just empty your head

579
00:29:59,422 --> 00:30:01,883
and trust it'll end sooner or later.

580
00:30:04,302 --> 00:30:06,721
CHAE-MIN STOPS WALKING

581
00:30:11,726 --> 00:30:12,560
Dowoon.

582
00:30:13,728 --> 00:30:14,979
Do you see that round tomb?

583
00:30:15,563 --> 00:30:16,981
The one hidden by the tree?

584
00:30:17,065 --> 00:30:18,441
Right in front here.

585
00:30:18,525 --> 00:30:19,859
-This one.
-It's a tomb?

586
00:30:19,943 --> 00:30:20,819
-You see that?
-Yeah.

587
00:30:20,902 --> 00:30:24,823
They say it's a stone tomb for those
who were bitten and killed by a tiger.

588
00:30:24,906 --> 00:30:25,949
Really?

589
00:30:26,032 --> 00:30:26,991
They're buried here.

590
00:30:28,368 --> 00:30:30,328
So tigers appear here.

591
00:30:30,411 --> 00:30:31,246
I guess so.

592
00:30:32,622 --> 00:30:33,456
HOSIKCHONG TOMBS

593
00:30:33,540 --> 00:30:35,834
A GRAVE FOR PEOPLE BITTEN
AND KILLED BY TIGERS

594
00:30:35,917 --> 00:30:39,546
PRECIOUS FOLK MATERIAL SHOWING A GLIMPSE
OF LIVES AND BELIEFS OF PEOPLE OF THE PAST

595
00:30:39,629 --> 00:30:41,589
It's so sad they were
bitten to death by tigers.

596
00:30:42,173 --> 00:30:43,341
Did you see Hosikchong?

597
00:30:43,424 --> 00:30:44,259
Yes.

598
00:30:44,342 --> 00:30:46,010
Are there tigers in Taebaeksan?

599
00:30:46,094 --> 00:30:47,554
I guess tigers used to live here.

600
00:30:47,637 --> 00:30:48,972
Not now though, right?

601
00:30:49,055 --> 00:30:50,807
There aren't any here now.

602
00:30:50,890 --> 00:30:52,851
What should you do
if you run into one here?

603
00:30:53,560 --> 00:30:55,270
When you see a tiger,

604
00:30:55,353 --> 00:30:56,980
should you pretend not to see it?

605
00:30:58,481 --> 00:31:00,608
Just ignore the wild animals.

606
00:31:00,692 --> 00:31:02,026
-Sorry?
-Ignore them.

607
00:31:02,110 --> 00:31:03,486
Ignore them?

608
00:31:04,529 --> 00:31:06,447
So if a wild boar is in front of me,

609
00:31:06,531 --> 00:31:07,490
I should…

610
00:31:07,574 --> 00:31:09,534
THEY LEARNED THIS DURING THEIR LESSON

611
00:31:09,617 --> 00:31:10,910
I should do this?

612
00:31:10,994 --> 00:31:12,078
THE DOCENT IS ON STANDBY

613
00:31:12,161 --> 00:31:16,749
At this location, there's something called
"The Amazing Green Carpet Moss."

614
00:31:16,833 --> 00:31:18,751
It's covered in snow,
so it's hard to see now.

615
00:31:18,835 --> 00:31:22,005
But there's a bunch of moss here
that goes all the way up.

616
00:31:23,464 --> 00:31:25,008
-So…
-Yes?

617
00:31:25,091 --> 00:31:26,217
I'm sorry,

618
00:31:27,051 --> 00:31:29,012
but we can't see the moss at all

619
00:31:29,095 --> 00:31:30,430
since it's covered in snow.

620
00:31:31,139 --> 00:31:32,682
So why are you explaining it?

621
00:31:32,765 --> 00:31:33,725
Oh, there it is.

622
00:31:33,808 --> 00:31:34,934
Yes.

623
00:31:35,018 --> 00:31:35,935
Is it this?

624
00:31:36,019 --> 00:31:37,478
So it's not just any moss?

625
00:31:37,562 --> 00:31:39,814
Yes, it's called "green carpet moss."

626
00:31:39,898 --> 00:31:41,900
It spreads all the way up there.

627
00:31:41,983 --> 00:31:45,194
FACT
IT'S JUST MOSS

628
00:31:45,278 --> 00:31:48,156
Then, is it different from normal moss?

629
00:31:48,239 --> 00:31:49,073
I need to check.

630
00:31:49,157 --> 00:31:50,450
Isn't this like

631
00:31:51,034 --> 00:31:53,870
educational material you turn on
for elementary school students?

632
00:31:53,953 --> 00:31:54,996
The EBS channel.

633
00:31:55,079 --> 00:31:57,373
If you think about it,
kids would like you lot.

634
00:31:57,457 --> 00:31:58,291
You're right.

635
00:31:58,374 --> 00:32:00,209
Are you sending this video file to EBS?

636
00:32:00,919 --> 00:32:03,922
It turns out this show
is for EBS, not Netflix.

637
00:32:04,005 --> 00:32:06,341
I think you'd be capable of such a lie.

638
00:32:07,800 --> 00:32:09,010
He keeps breaking the flow.

639
00:32:10,386 --> 00:32:11,220
LAUGHING

640
00:32:11,304 --> 00:32:12,138
The flow…

641
00:32:12,221 --> 00:32:16,017
We'd still be climbing up
Seoraksan at this time.

642
00:32:16,100 --> 00:32:16,935
Exactly.

643
00:32:17,018 --> 00:32:18,144
How did we do it?

644
00:32:18,227 --> 00:32:19,312
It's scary to think about.

645
00:32:19,395 --> 00:32:20,939
I'm amazed that we did it.

646
00:32:21,522 --> 00:32:23,691
Seriously, how did we hike there?

647
00:32:23,775 --> 00:32:26,653
But if the first mountain was Taebaeksan,

648
00:32:27,612 --> 00:32:29,280
and the second one was Seoraksan,

649
00:32:29,364 --> 00:32:30,531
it would've felt even harder.

650
00:32:30,615 --> 00:32:31,532
I agree.

651
00:32:32,867 --> 00:32:34,243
They planned the order well.

652
00:32:35,620 --> 00:32:37,830
Are they going to take us
to Baekdusan next?

653
00:32:38,498 --> 00:32:40,541
I really want to go to a hot spring.

654
00:32:40,625 --> 00:32:42,502
AS THEY TALK ABOUT THIS AND THAT

655
00:32:42,585 --> 00:32:44,712
Seriously, the next time we go somewhere…

656
00:32:44,796 --> 00:32:47,382
-We should go.
-We have to go if they have one.

657
00:32:48,675 --> 00:32:50,134
We must be almost all the way down.

658
00:32:50,218 --> 00:32:51,678
-We're almost done.
-We're here.

659
00:32:51,761 --> 00:32:53,513
I see houses.

660
00:32:55,181 --> 00:32:56,516
I see a greenhouse.

661
00:32:57,016 --> 00:32:59,018
You worked so hard, Jung-won.

662
00:32:59,102 --> 00:33:01,187
-Really.
-No, you guys worked hard.

663
00:33:01,688 --> 00:33:03,940
Jung-won, we'll see you
on the next filming day, right?

664
00:33:04,023 --> 00:33:05,900
COUGHING

665
00:33:06,609 --> 00:33:07,527
LAUGHING

666
00:33:07,610 --> 00:33:09,195
Is today our last day together?

667
00:33:09,278 --> 00:33:11,072
Let's do a heartfelt goodbye just in case.

668
00:33:11,155 --> 00:33:12,699
Later, when we say goodbye…

669
00:33:13,241 --> 00:33:15,034
-Let's do a proper one.
-Yes, just in case.

670
00:33:15,118 --> 00:33:16,536
-We'll hug and everything.
-Yeah.

671
00:33:17,829 --> 00:33:20,164
We could see each other somewhere else.

672
00:33:21,040 --> 00:33:22,417
We could meet happily.

673
00:33:23,710 --> 00:33:25,795
I feel like I have
some stamina left today.

674
00:33:26,504 --> 00:33:27,422
Don't say that.

675
00:33:28,089 --> 00:33:30,508
Just say you spent
the right amount. Sorry?

676
00:33:31,342 --> 00:33:32,176
Don't say that.

677
00:33:32,802 --> 00:33:34,637
Just say you spent
the right amount. Sorry?

678
00:33:34,721 --> 00:33:36,264
-You have energy left?
-No, we're good.

679
00:33:36,347 --> 00:33:38,141
It's enough energy to eat

680
00:33:38,224 --> 00:33:39,559
and lift the spoon.

681
00:33:39,642 --> 00:33:40,935
Enough to chat while eating--

682
00:33:41,019 --> 00:33:43,855
Want to go for another hike?
There's Hambaeksan next to this one.

683
00:33:43,938 --> 00:33:44,814
No.

684
00:33:45,606 --> 00:33:47,066
Want to go see the sun glow at dusk?

685
00:33:47,150 --> 00:33:48,151
No.

686
00:33:48,234 --> 00:33:49,360
Want to see the sunset?

687
00:33:49,444 --> 00:33:50,403
No.

688
00:33:50,486 --> 00:33:52,530
I want to see the sunset in Seoul.

689
00:33:53,281 --> 00:33:54,323
ARRIVAL AT DANGGOL PLAZA

690
00:33:54,407 --> 00:33:56,117
I'll see it from N Seoul Tower.

691
00:33:56,200 --> 00:33:57,702
I'll take the elevator.

692
00:33:58,286 --> 00:34:01,664
We've arrived at Danggol Plaza.

693
00:34:03,082 --> 00:34:03,916
HIKE FINISHED

694
00:34:04,000 --> 00:34:06,044
-The descent is complete.
-Good work, everyone.

695
00:34:06,127 --> 00:34:07,545
We'll go and eat now.

696
00:34:07,628 --> 00:34:09,797
-Okay.
-This is The Mountaineer's Oath.

697
00:34:11,966 --> 00:34:13,509
Should we read it before we go?

698
00:34:13,593 --> 00:34:14,427
Could you…

699
00:34:14,510 --> 00:34:17,221
AN ENGRAVED STONE STANDING ALONE

700
00:34:17,305 --> 00:34:19,223
THE MOUNTAINEER'S OATH
BY NOSAN LEE EUN-SANG

701
00:34:19,307 --> 00:34:21,684
Could you recite it for us, President Tar?

702
00:34:21,768 --> 00:34:23,061
You should take the oath.

703
00:34:23,144 --> 00:34:24,896
"The Mountaineer's Oath."

704
00:34:24,979 --> 00:34:26,272
-I swear.
-I swear.

705
00:34:26,355 --> 00:34:27,190
I swear.

706
00:34:27,273 --> 00:34:32,278
"Mountaineers explore
the endless universe."

707
00:34:32,361 --> 00:34:34,155
"Until we arrive at the destination,

708
00:34:34,238 --> 00:34:37,617
we will overcome all hardships
through passion and cooperation."

709
00:34:37,700 --> 00:34:39,535
"Until we arrive at the destination,

710
00:34:39,619 --> 00:34:42,914
we will overcome all hardships
through passion and cooperation."

711
00:34:42,997 --> 00:34:48,127
"We will never despair nor give up."

712
00:34:48,211 --> 00:34:50,671
Why is it so funny when you read that?

713
00:34:50,755 --> 00:34:55,885
"Mountaineers
must assimilate with nature."

714
00:34:55,968 --> 00:35:00,348
"Without deception or pretense."

715
00:35:00,431 --> 00:35:07,021
"But to the world
of true freedom, peace, and love."

716
00:35:07,105 --> 00:35:10,775
"We will march toward it."

717
00:35:10,858 --> 00:35:12,276
The words were really moving.

718
00:35:12,360 --> 00:35:13,778
THE OATH MOVES MOUNTAINEERS' HEARTS

719
00:35:13,861 --> 00:35:15,655
-Anyway, good job.
-Thank you.

720
00:35:15,738 --> 00:35:17,115
You did great work hiking.

721
00:35:17,198 --> 00:35:18,574
Good job, everyone.

722
00:35:19,867 --> 00:35:23,079
The oath was rather meaningful to me.

723
00:35:25,873 --> 00:35:28,292
I could speak in a loud voice
for the first time.

724
00:35:30,711 --> 00:35:34,298
HOW DID IT FEEL TO HIKE TAEBAEKSAN?

725
00:35:35,299 --> 00:35:39,971
That was exactly how I'd imagined
a mountain view would look,

726
00:35:40,054 --> 00:35:42,140
not like Seoraksan's.

727
00:35:42,682 --> 00:35:45,935
That's my personal preference
if I have to compare the two.

728
00:35:46,769 --> 00:35:48,813
But it was so cold.

729
00:35:49,564 --> 00:35:51,065
I'm serious.

730
00:35:51,149 --> 00:35:54,485
It was really cold when we filmed
the music video for "Famous."

731
00:35:54,569 --> 00:35:57,446
That was one of the coldest days
of my life.

732
00:35:58,281 --> 00:36:00,491
But this set a new record for cold.

733
00:36:00,575 --> 00:36:03,661
Maybe I should gain some weight for this.

734
00:36:04,871 --> 00:36:06,998
WHICH MOUNTAIN WAS EASIER?
TAEBAEKSAN OR SEORAKSAN?

735
00:36:07,081 --> 00:36:08,875
I'd still say Taebaeksan.

736
00:36:09,584 --> 00:36:10,960
Who would choose Seoraksan?

737
00:36:13,254 --> 00:36:14,755
Why on earth do people hike?

738
00:36:17,300 --> 00:36:18,593
I think I'll be reminded of this

739
00:36:20,052 --> 00:36:22,722
on days when I wake up early
and don't go hiking.

740
00:36:22,805 --> 00:36:23,681
We keep…

741
00:36:25,016 --> 00:36:26,893
starting hikes in an unhealthy way.

742
00:36:27,393 --> 00:36:29,228
I still don't know
why on earth people hike.

743
00:36:30,229 --> 00:36:31,981
Honestly, I still don't know yet.

744
00:36:33,566 --> 00:36:37,403
I still don't understand
why people use only their legs to walk up.

745
00:36:37,486 --> 00:36:40,281
You should ride a snowmobile,

746
00:36:40,364 --> 00:36:42,533
walk about 50 m,

747
00:36:42,617 --> 00:36:44,160
take a photo,

748
00:36:44,243 --> 00:36:45,703
put your helmet back on,

749
00:36:45,786 --> 00:36:48,664
and ride back down on the snowmobile.

750
00:36:48,748 --> 00:36:49,999
That would be fun.

751
00:36:50,082 --> 00:36:52,877
Why on earth do you think people hike?

752
00:36:56,881 --> 00:36:58,633
I'll only know if we do more of the show.

753
00:37:00,676 --> 00:37:02,428
We'll be hiking more mountains anyway.

754
00:37:02,511 --> 00:37:04,388
Right? Let's hike some more and see.

755
00:37:04,472 --> 00:37:05,765
We'll hike some more,

756
00:37:05,848 --> 00:37:10,478
and I'll decide if I want
to cut ties with mountains later.

757
00:37:10,561 --> 00:37:11,729
I feel like

758
00:37:11,812 --> 00:37:14,065
you're the person
who is best suited for mountains.

759
00:37:14,148 --> 00:37:14,982
Me?

760
00:37:16,025 --> 00:37:17,652
That was the loudest I've spoken today.

761
00:37:21,697 --> 00:37:22,865
SEORAKSAN TRAINING

762
00:37:22,949 --> 00:37:24,492
WATCHING THE SUNRISE ON TAEBAEKSAN

763
00:37:29,705 --> 00:37:31,374
My leg muscles are all stiff right now.

764
00:37:31,457 --> 00:37:32,708
THEY'RE GOING TO GO TO EAT NOW

765
00:37:32,792 --> 00:37:34,001
See you soon.

766
00:37:35,294 --> 00:37:36,504
Geez.

767
00:37:36,587 --> 00:37:38,089
THEY CAN'T HELP BUT MOAN

768
00:37:39,840 --> 00:37:42,468
AS SOON AS HE SITS
HE OPENS UP TO YAWN WITH NO RESISTANCE

769
00:37:43,344 --> 00:37:45,763
-Good night.
-Good night.

770
00:37:45,846 --> 00:37:47,890
EVERYONE FALLS ASLEEP

771
00:37:48,474 --> 00:37:50,768
PERHAPS DREAMING OF HIKING?

772
00:37:51,519 --> 00:37:54,021
MEANWHILE, THE BUS LEAVES TAEBAEKSAN

773
00:37:54,855 --> 00:37:56,983
IT DRIVES INTO THE CITY

774
00:37:57,066 --> 00:37:58,693
AND ARRIVES AT THE RESTAURANT

775
00:37:58,776 --> 00:38:00,278
We'll get off the bus now.

776
00:38:01,529 --> 00:38:03,823
ALREADY?

777
00:38:03,906 --> 00:38:07,034
I fell asleep as soon as I closed my eyes.

778
00:38:07,618 --> 00:38:08,786
GASPS

779
00:38:09,912 --> 00:38:11,998
THE TERRIBLE AFTEREFFECTS OF HIKING

780
00:38:13,708 --> 00:38:16,252
DESCEND CLUB ARRIVES AT…

781
00:38:16,335 --> 00:38:18,963
This is a famous place
that was on <i>Huh Young-man's Food Travel.</i>

782
00:38:19,046 --> 00:38:19,964
MODERN DINER

783
00:38:20,047 --> 00:38:21,590
A FAMOUS RESTAURANT IN TAEBAEK

784
00:38:23,134 --> 00:38:25,094
THE RESTAURANT'S MAIN DISH

785
00:38:31,183 --> 00:38:33,102
HIGH-QUALITY KOREAN BEEF FROM TAEBAEK

786
00:38:33,185 --> 00:38:36,147
THE KEY IS TO GRILL USING BRIQUETTES
LIKE MINERS BEFORE THE 1990S

787
00:38:46,657 --> 00:38:48,868
THE SMOKY SCENT OF THE GRILL

788
00:38:50,995 --> 00:38:53,414
WITH SWEET AND SALTY BEEF TARTARE
ON THE SIDE

789
00:38:54,040 --> 00:38:55,082
Gosh.

790
00:38:56,751 --> 00:38:58,961
DESCEND CLUB ENTERS

791
00:38:59,587 --> 00:39:01,756
It's one of the best 100 restaurants
in Korea.

792
00:39:01,839 --> 00:39:04,091
-Right.
-We should try it out.

793
00:39:04,175 --> 00:39:06,052
Shall we order
assorted beef and beef tartare?

794
00:39:06,135 --> 00:39:06,969
-Sure.
-Sure.

795
00:39:07,053 --> 00:39:08,220
PRESIDENT TAR MAKES THE ORDER

796
00:39:08,304 --> 00:39:10,431
-Gosh.
-Geez.

797
00:39:10,514 --> 00:39:11,515
I want to go to Seoul.

798
00:39:11,599 --> 00:39:12,975
How will I do my shoot tomorrow?

799
00:39:13,059 --> 00:39:14,602
WORRIED ABOUT TOMORROW DUE TO SORENESS

800
00:39:14,685 --> 00:39:17,438
I should go home and sit
in the massage chair for two hours.

801
00:39:17,521 --> 00:39:18,606
I'll use my leg massagers.

802
00:39:19,315 --> 00:39:20,983
AS THEY MAKE PLANS FOR RECOVERY

803
00:39:21,067 --> 00:39:23,194
THEIR ORDERED FOOD ARRIVES

804
00:39:23,277 --> 00:39:24,862
The meat is good quality here.

805
00:39:24,945 --> 00:39:26,530
Taebaek is famous for its beef.

806
00:39:26,614 --> 00:39:28,157
HE CAN'T TAKE HIS EYES OFF OF IT

807
00:39:28,240 --> 00:39:30,034
-I'll grill the meat.
-Okay.

808
00:39:30,117 --> 00:39:31,827
I'll grill it very lightly.

809
00:39:31,911 --> 00:39:32,828
CHAE-MIN WILL COOK

810
00:39:32,912 --> 00:39:33,913
-Thanks.
-I like it rare.

811
00:39:33,996 --> 00:39:35,748
-I'll start right away.
-Okay.

812
00:39:35,831 --> 00:39:36,999
Have some beef tartare first.

813
00:39:37,083 --> 00:39:37,917
Should I?

814
00:39:38,000 --> 00:39:39,168
BEEF TARTARE AS AN APPETIZER

815
00:39:39,251 --> 00:39:40,795
I've often seen redder ones.

816
00:39:40,878 --> 00:39:41,962
It's salty but it's good.

817
00:39:42,046 --> 00:39:43,172
THEIR FIRST MEAL IN 9 HOURS

818
00:39:43,255 --> 00:39:45,049
This beef tartare is so good.

819
00:39:45,132 --> 00:39:46,217
Eat up.

820
00:39:46,884 --> 00:39:48,177
YUM

821
00:39:48,260 --> 00:39:50,679
I've never seen this kind of color before.

822
00:39:51,514 --> 00:39:53,057
TAKES ANOTHER BITE

823
00:39:53,140 --> 00:39:54,392
This beef tartare is insane.

824
00:39:55,101 --> 00:39:56,435
It's a bit spicy too.

825
00:40:01,982 --> 00:40:04,485
THE OLDER MEMBERS TAKE A BITE TOO

826
00:40:05,486 --> 00:40:07,363
Pass me some tongs. Let's cook together.

827
00:40:07,446 --> 00:40:09,156
ASSISTANT: TARZZAN

828
00:40:09,240 --> 00:40:11,242
THEY START GRILLING NOW

829
00:40:22,878 --> 00:40:27,133
ADDING SMOKY FLAVOR FROM THE BRIQUETTES

830
00:40:28,050 --> 00:40:29,927
The meat here is really good.

831
00:40:30,010 --> 00:40:30,970
The meat is good.

832
00:40:32,221 --> 00:40:33,180
I won't ruin it.

833
00:40:34,265 --> 00:40:35,558
I think we can eat these.

834
00:40:35,641 --> 00:40:36,725
-So go ahead?
-They're rare.

835
00:40:45,067 --> 00:40:46,318
Please eat up.

836
00:40:50,739 --> 00:40:51,615
YUM

837
00:40:51,699 --> 00:40:52,867
-Gosh.
-Gosh.

838
00:40:52,950 --> 00:40:54,869
THE COOKS ARE SATISFIED

839
00:40:59,331 --> 00:41:00,291
It's delicious.

840
00:41:02,251 --> 00:41:04,920
DIPPING IT IN SALT

841
00:41:06,755 --> 00:41:08,424
This is so good.

842
00:41:09,842 --> 00:41:11,594
Now, this is it.

843
00:41:16,056 --> 00:41:17,808
HE WAS TOO HASTY

844
00:41:17,892 --> 00:41:19,185
COUGHING

845
00:41:20,019 --> 00:41:22,897
THEY KEEP GRILLING THE MEAT NONSTOP

846
00:41:34,408 --> 00:41:35,242
Chae-min.

847
00:41:35,326 --> 00:41:37,286
-You eat it.
-No, hurry. The sauce is spilling.

848
00:41:37,369 --> 00:41:38,496
YOU FIRST
NO, YOU FIRST

849
00:41:38,579 --> 00:41:39,455
There you go.

850
00:41:41,707 --> 00:41:44,376
EATING CAREFULLY THIS TIME

851
00:41:49,048 --> 00:41:49,882
Gosh.

852
00:41:50,633 --> 00:41:51,800
It sure tastes good.

853
00:41:51,884 --> 00:41:53,344
Everyone's eating a lot.

854
00:41:53,844 --> 00:41:54,678
We have to eat up.

855
00:41:54,762 --> 00:41:56,555
-Having this much beef is rare.
-Right.

856
00:41:56,639 --> 00:41:57,473
DESCEND CLUB RULE

857
00:41:57,556 --> 00:41:59,391
WHEN HIKING IS COMPLETE,
FREE FOOD IS PROVIDED

858
00:41:59,475 --> 00:42:01,393
THEY ATE THEIR FILL
WITH PRODUCTION'S MONEY

859
00:42:01,477 --> 00:42:03,896
I'm starting to feel sleepy.

860
00:42:03,979 --> 00:42:04,813
Me too.

861
00:42:04,897 --> 00:42:06,023
That's normal.

862
00:42:06,732 --> 00:42:07,775
That's right.

863
00:42:07,858 --> 00:42:10,986
I hate the term "normal" now
because it sounds like "summit."

864
00:42:11,695 --> 00:42:14,031
AVERSION TO NORMALCY AND SUMMITS

865
00:42:14,114 --> 00:42:16,909
How long were we at the summit for?

866
00:42:17,409 --> 00:42:18,369
About five minutes?

867
00:42:18,869 --> 00:42:20,329
We couldn't stay there for long.

868
00:42:20,412 --> 00:42:21,914
It was too windy.

869
00:42:21,997 --> 00:42:24,458
We ate the energy bars, took photos,
and came down.

870
00:42:24,542 --> 00:42:26,126
BEFITTING OF THE NAME "DESCEND CLUB"

871
00:42:26,210 --> 00:42:27,920
The energy bar was so delicious.

872
00:42:28,003 --> 00:42:29,797
That's why I told you to eat it.

873
00:42:29,880 --> 00:42:30,714
FRUSTRATED

874
00:42:30,798 --> 00:42:32,007
I'll listen to you guys now.

875
00:42:32,091 --> 00:42:34,426
If you tell me to eat something,
I'll eat it.

876
00:42:34,510 --> 00:42:35,344
MATURED GARDEN

877
00:42:35,427 --> 00:42:37,930
Do you prefer Seoraksan or Taebaeksan?

878
00:42:38,013 --> 00:42:39,098
-Taebaeksan.
-Taebaeksan.

879
00:42:40,057 --> 00:42:41,225
Who would want to walk

880
00:42:41,308 --> 00:42:44,186
on a mountain for ten hours?

881
00:42:44,270 --> 00:42:45,771
THE 9 HOURS 32 MINUTES ON SEORAKSAN

882
00:42:45,854 --> 00:42:46,939
It was like taking an exam.

883
00:42:47,022 --> 00:42:49,858
The time taken for this one
was just right.

884
00:42:49,942 --> 00:42:51,777
If it weren't for the time limit,

885
00:42:51,860 --> 00:42:54,780
you could've taken your time to hike,
and it would've been fine.

886
00:42:54,863 --> 00:42:56,156
NODDING

887
00:42:56,240 --> 00:42:58,742
You had to make it before sunrise,
so you didn't stop.

888
00:42:58,826 --> 00:42:59,827
THE YOUNGER MEMBERS NOD

889
00:42:59,910 --> 00:43:00,911
We were hasty at first.

890
00:43:00,995 --> 00:43:02,037
You become impatient.

891
00:43:02,121 --> 00:43:03,247
MOUNTAIN ALLERGY TRIGGERED

892
00:43:03,330 --> 00:43:04,331
If it weren't for that…

893
00:43:04,415 --> 00:43:05,916
Yes, it'd feel like a picnic.

894
00:43:06,000 --> 00:43:07,960
A WORD FROM THE FOREIGN AFFAIRS MINISTER

895
00:43:08,043 --> 00:43:10,504
I can already picture
the press conference for the premiere.

896
00:43:10,588 --> 00:43:12,840
A reporter asks, "Who's the best?"
And I say Chae-min.

897
00:43:12,923 --> 00:43:14,341
PRODUCER NAH PLANS AHEAD BY HIMSELF

898
00:43:14,425 --> 00:43:16,510
I promise you. I'm not lying.

899
00:43:16,594 --> 00:43:18,178
I won't be at the press conference.

900
00:43:18,971 --> 00:43:20,222
I promise you.

901
00:43:20,306 --> 00:43:21,140
SHOCKING DECLARATION

902
00:43:21,223 --> 00:43:24,935
Jung-won,
I kind of missed this side of you.

903
00:43:25,019 --> 00:43:27,146
You were way too positive while hiking.

904
00:43:28,897 --> 00:43:31,400
Right, I should reveal the second quest.

905
00:43:31,483 --> 00:43:33,652
Today's first quest

906
00:43:33,736 --> 00:43:35,529
was seeing the sunrise on Taebaeksan.

907
00:43:35,613 --> 00:43:39,116
All of you saw the sunrise.
Congratulations. You cleared the quest.

908
00:43:39,199 --> 00:43:41,535
FIRST QUEST COMPLETE

909
00:43:41,619 --> 00:43:43,329
FEELING PROUD

910
00:43:43,412 --> 00:43:45,164
Here's the 25 km badge.

911
00:43:45,247 --> 00:43:46,332
It was 25 km?

912
00:43:46,415 --> 00:43:47,583
We walked 25 km today?

913
00:43:48,959 --> 00:43:49,877
Seoraksan was 17 km.

914
00:43:49,960 --> 00:43:51,003
SEORAKSAN
17 KM ROUND TRIP

915
00:43:51,086 --> 00:43:58,052
TAEBAEKSAN

916
00:44:00,137 --> 00:44:01,722
8 KM ROUND TRIP

917
00:44:01,805 --> 00:44:03,557
SEORAKSAN, 17 KM
PLUS TAEBAEKSAN, 8 KM

918
00:44:03,641 --> 00:44:05,601
TOTAL 25 KM WALKED

919
00:44:05,684 --> 00:44:07,603
So we walked a total of 25 km?

920
00:44:07,686 --> 00:44:09,563
-Yes.
-We'll hit 100 km quickly.

921
00:44:10,314 --> 00:44:12,149
Have you prepared the next show?

922
00:44:12,232 --> 00:44:13,984
HE'LL CHANGE THE SHOW
IF THEY GO OVER 100 KM

923
00:44:14,068 --> 00:44:16,236
The second quest will now be revealed.

924
00:44:19,281 --> 00:44:21,241
SIGHING

925
00:44:21,325 --> 00:44:22,534
The second quest

926
00:44:25,079 --> 00:44:27,456
is Baengnokdam Crater Lake
at Hallasan Mountain.

927
00:44:28,415 --> 00:44:29,583
Goodbye!

928
00:44:31,502 --> 00:44:32,670
Baengnokdam Crater Lake.

929
00:44:33,671 --> 00:44:34,838
Goodbye!

930
00:44:34,922 --> 00:44:36,382
1,950 M ABOVE SEA LEVEL

931
00:44:36,465 --> 00:44:40,552
HALLASAN IS THE HIGHEST MOUNTAIN IN KOREA

932
00:44:43,806 --> 00:44:45,140
VERY TOUGH FOR BEGINNER HIKERS

933
00:44:45,224 --> 00:44:47,476
I somewhat expected it,
but you're doing exactly that.

934
00:44:48,727 --> 00:44:50,354
I thought this would be our last quest.

935
00:44:50,437 --> 00:44:52,189
DRONE FILMING WAS ALLOWED AFTER DISCUSSION

936
00:44:52,272 --> 00:44:53,774
WITH HALLASAN NATIONAL PARK

937
00:44:53,857 --> 00:44:55,192
HALLASAN

938
00:44:56,193 --> 00:44:59,321
RISING FROM THE CENTER OF JEJU ISLAND

939
00:44:59,405 --> 00:45:02,032
IS A MOUNTAIN WITH AN ELEVATION OF 1,950 M

940
00:45:03,075 --> 00:45:09,081
HIGHER THAN THE CLOUDS
AND CLOSEST TO THE SKY

941
00:45:11,708 --> 00:45:15,462
SHAPED OVER TIME BY NATURE

942
00:45:17,965 --> 00:45:24,930
THE HABITAT OF VARIOUS ORGANISMS

943
00:45:26,306 --> 00:45:28,976
AND THE TOP OF HALLASAN

944
00:45:30,060 --> 00:45:35,899
BAENGNOKDAM

945
00:45:42,823 --> 00:45:48,078
MANY MOUNTAINEERS DREAM
TO SEE THIS LANDSCAPE

946
00:45:49,830 --> 00:45:53,375
BUT DUE TO THE EVER-CHANGING CLOUDS

947
00:45:53,459 --> 00:45:56,336
AND THE FREQUENT FOG THAT COVERS IT

948
00:45:59,506 --> 00:46:02,050
THEY SAY YOU NEED
THREE GENERATIONS OF LUCK

949
00:46:02,134 --> 00:46:03,302
TO CLEARLY SEE BAENGNOKDAM

950
00:46:06,763 --> 00:46:08,807
DRONE FILMING WAS ALLOWED AFTER DISCUSSION

951
00:46:08,891 --> 00:46:10,893
WITH HALLASAN NATIONAL PARK

952
00:46:10,976 --> 00:46:12,269
2ND QUEST
BAENGNOKDAM, HALLASAN

953
00:46:12,352 --> 00:46:13,312
So, with Hallasan…

954
00:46:13,395 --> 00:46:14,813
Let him talk first.

955
00:46:14,897 --> 00:46:16,190
Let him talk.

956
00:46:17,191 --> 00:46:19,735
We need to leave today anyway.

957
00:46:19,818 --> 00:46:20,736
HE WANTS TO LEAVE NOW

958
00:46:20,819 --> 00:46:22,070
So let him talk first.

959
00:46:22,154 --> 00:46:23,405
Hallasan?

960
00:46:25,782 --> 00:46:26,867
Hallasan?

961
00:46:27,534 --> 00:46:28,869
How bad is Hallasan?

962
00:46:28,952 --> 00:46:30,287
When compared to Seoraksan?

963
00:46:30,370 --> 00:46:32,581
I heard it's better than Seoraksan.

964
00:46:32,664 --> 00:46:34,708
It's slightly easier.

965
00:46:34,791 --> 00:46:36,877
THE SLOPE IS LOWER AND THE PATH IS LONGER

966
00:46:36,960 --> 00:46:38,879
We'll suffer when we descend.

967
00:46:38,962 --> 00:46:40,672
HE WORRIES ABOUT DESCENDING FIRST

968
00:46:40,756 --> 00:46:41,590
WORRIED ABOUT WIND

969
00:46:41,673 --> 00:46:42,925
Jeju Island will be very windy.

970
00:46:43,008 --> 00:46:43,884
AND ALTITUDE SICKNESS

971
00:46:43,967 --> 00:46:45,219
Elevation is 1,950 m.

972
00:46:45,302 --> 00:46:46,303
FULL OF CONCERNS

973
00:46:46,386 --> 00:46:47,721
We heard him out.

974
00:46:48,889 --> 00:46:50,641
-Let's go home.
-Let's think about it.

975
00:46:50,724 --> 00:46:52,601
It'll be for three days and two nights.

976
00:46:54,811 --> 00:46:56,355
We hike one day… I mean rest one day.

977
00:46:56,438 --> 00:46:57,814
HE'S CURIOUS ABOUT THE SCHEDULE

978
00:46:57,898 --> 00:46:59,233
Then, hike one day…

979
00:46:59,983 --> 00:47:00,817
Chae-min.

980
00:47:01,568 --> 00:47:03,028
SHUSH

981
00:47:03,111 --> 00:47:05,864
LET'S STOP HERE TODAY

982
00:47:05,948 --> 00:47:06,782
Let's go.

983
00:47:06,865 --> 00:47:08,075
Okay.

984
00:47:08,158 --> 00:47:11,078
AFTER THE FIRST SHOOT ENDS

985
00:47:11,662 --> 00:47:12,621
You look like brothers.

986
00:47:12,704 --> 00:47:15,207
GO-HOME GARDEN IS HAPPY NOW

987
00:47:15,290 --> 00:47:16,625
-Good job.
-Take care.

988
00:47:16,708 --> 00:47:17,876
Please go to the hospital.

989
00:47:18,377 --> 00:47:19,211
See you.

990
00:47:19,795 --> 00:47:21,296
-Bye.
-Good job today.

991
00:47:21,380 --> 00:47:23,382
-See you next week.
-Thank you.

992
00:47:23,465 --> 00:47:24,633
-Take care.
-Bye.

993
00:47:24,716 --> 00:47:26,843
-Have a safe flight.
-Thank you.

994
00:47:26,927 --> 00:47:29,096
DOWOON LEAVES TOO

995
00:47:29,179 --> 00:47:30,764
I knew I'd be the last one to go.

996
00:47:31,390 --> 00:47:32,224
CHAE-MIN IS ALONE

997
00:47:32,307 --> 00:47:33,392
I knew I'd be the last one.

998
00:47:33,475 --> 00:47:34,685
Our camera operator said

999
00:47:35,310 --> 00:47:36,186
you kept smiling.

1000
00:47:37,145 --> 00:47:37,980
He was smiling.

1001
00:47:38,063 --> 00:47:40,107
It was funny how the older members
were struggling.

1002
00:47:40,190 --> 00:47:41,817
JOKING

1003
00:47:41,900 --> 00:47:42,734
They're cute.

1004
00:47:42,818 --> 00:47:44,653
Rather than funny, they're cute.

1005
00:47:44,736 --> 00:47:46,488
THE NEXT DAY

1006
00:47:46,572 --> 00:47:47,990
DOWOON
HOW ARE YOUR LEGS?

1007
00:47:48,073 --> 00:47:50,075
CAR, THE GARDEN
A BIT BETTER

1008
00:47:50,158 --> 00:47:54,496
DOWOON
HANG IN THERE

1009
00:47:54,580 --> 00:47:57,874
CHAE-MIN
I NEED TO RELEARN HOW TO HOLD POLES

1010
00:47:58,792 --> 00:48:02,004
CHAE-MIN INJURED HIS WRIST

1011
00:48:02,087 --> 00:48:03,839
CAR, THE GARDEN
GOSH… GET WELL SOON!

1012
00:48:03,922 --> 00:48:05,090
DOWOON
OH, DEAR

1013
00:48:05,173 --> 00:48:06,466
CHAE-MIN
HANG IN THERE, EVERYONE!

1014
00:48:06,550 --> 00:48:09,219
TARZZAN
HANG IN THERE, EVERYONE!

1015
00:48:09,303 --> 00:48:11,430
I'M BRINGING VERY SWEET HIKING SNACKS
FROM THE US

1016
00:48:11,513 --> 00:48:12,848
CAR, THE GARDEN
SEE YOU SOON

1017
00:48:12,931 --> 00:48:14,224
DOWOON
YEAH, GET WELL SOON

1018
00:48:14,308 --> 00:48:16,852
CHAE-MIN
I'LL DO MY BEST!

1019
00:48:16,935 --> 00:48:19,021
A FEW DAYS LATER

1020
00:48:20,689 --> 00:48:22,858
THE DAY THEY GO TO JEJU ISLAND

1021
00:48:23,692 --> 00:48:26,361
GANGNAM, SEOUL

1022
00:48:28,113 --> 00:48:29,031
Hello.

1023
00:48:29,114 --> 00:48:31,617
DOWOON ARRIVES

1024
00:48:31,700 --> 00:48:33,285
-How have you been?
-Good.

1025
00:48:33,368 --> 00:48:34,786
You seem to be in good condition.

1026
00:48:34,870 --> 00:48:36,121
Now? Gosh.

1027
00:48:37,623 --> 00:48:38,957
THOUGHTS OF HIKING MAKE HIM SIGH

1028
00:48:39,041 --> 00:48:41,209
-We're not hiking yet.
-Of course not. That's good.

1029
00:48:41,293 --> 00:48:42,294
Am I the first to arrive?

1030
00:48:42,377 --> 00:48:43,378
You're here early.

1031
00:48:45,797 --> 00:48:49,468
THEY'LL ALL TAKE A BUS
TO GIMPO INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT

1032
00:48:50,594 --> 00:48:51,595
-President Tar.
-Hello.

1033
00:48:51,678 --> 00:48:53,138
-Hello, sir.
-Hello.

1034
00:48:53,221 --> 00:48:54,056
Hello.

1035
00:48:55,140 --> 00:48:56,433
I can tell you came from the US.

1036
00:48:56,516 --> 00:48:58,310
-Sorry?
-I can tell you're from the US.

1037
00:48:58,393 --> 00:48:59,978
TARZZAN WENT TO THE STATES RECENTLY

1038
00:49:00,062 --> 00:49:00,896
Tarzzan.

1039
00:49:00,979 --> 00:49:01,813
Hi.

1040
00:49:01,897 --> 00:49:02,981
Hello, Dowoon.

1041
00:49:05,317 --> 00:49:07,110
You're on TV so often these days.

1042
00:49:07,194 --> 00:49:08,320
Me? What do you mean?

1043
00:49:08,403 --> 00:49:10,238
My mother saw you on the show.

1044
00:49:10,322 --> 00:49:13,283
The one where you live alone.

1045
00:49:13,367 --> 00:49:14,451
Right.

1046
00:49:14,534 --> 00:49:18,163
DOWOON HIKED CHEONGGYESAN
ON ANOTHER SHOW TO SEE THE SUNRISE

1047
00:49:18,246 --> 00:49:20,165
I hiked Cheonggyesan in -10°C weather.

1048
00:49:20,248 --> 00:49:21,541
How was it?

1049
00:49:21,625 --> 00:49:24,836
After hiking with us,
did you develop any tricks?

1050
00:49:24,920 --> 00:49:27,214
Definitely. Cheonggyesan was so easy.

1051
00:49:27,297 --> 00:49:29,758
-Really?
-I took one hour to go up.

1052
00:49:29,841 --> 00:49:31,510
But Seoraksan was… Damn.

1053
00:49:32,594 --> 00:49:34,096
No, I just slept for five hours.

1054
00:49:34,179 --> 00:49:35,013
-You slept?
-Yes.

1055
00:49:35,097 --> 00:49:36,890
CHAE-MIN ARRIVES

1056
00:49:36,973 --> 00:49:38,141
-Hello.
-Hi.

1057
00:49:38,225 --> 00:49:39,559
-Hello.
-Hello.

1058
00:49:39,643 --> 00:49:41,061
Hello there.

1059
00:49:42,604 --> 00:49:44,648
A DEEP SIGH

1060
00:49:45,899 --> 00:49:47,734
Are the four of us going to sit here?

1061
00:49:47,818 --> 00:49:49,820
When Car-the comes,

1062
00:49:49,903 --> 00:49:51,113
it's going to be packed.

1063
00:49:51,947 --> 00:49:52,823
It'll be tight.

1064
00:49:52,906 --> 00:49:54,282
It'll look cute.

1065
00:49:54,366 --> 00:49:55,617
CAR-THE ARRIVES

1066
00:49:55,701 --> 00:49:56,535
I feel a bit…

1067
00:49:58,453 --> 00:49:59,287
Hold on.

1068
00:49:59,371 --> 00:50:01,456
I thought I'd feel better once I arrived.

1069
00:50:02,374 --> 00:50:03,375
Hello.

1070
00:50:03,458 --> 00:50:04,960
Hello, Jung-won.

1071
00:50:05,043 --> 00:50:05,961
Hi.

1072
00:50:06,044 --> 00:50:07,462
I made the stars wait.

1073
00:50:07,546 --> 00:50:08,588
Don't say that.

1074
00:50:09,798 --> 00:50:11,550
I haven't been
on this type of bus in ages.

1075
00:50:11,633 --> 00:50:13,969
ALL MEMBERS OF DESCEND CLUB ARE ABOARD

1076
00:50:14,052 --> 00:50:15,262
TO GIMPO INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT

1077
00:50:15,345 --> 00:50:16,847
Jeju Island has good food.

1078
00:50:16,930 --> 00:50:18,223
I'm looking forward to that.

1079
00:50:18,306 --> 00:50:20,684
I went straight to the hospital
the day I came back.

1080
00:50:20,767 --> 00:50:23,103
CAR, THE GARDEN WENT
TO THE HOSPITAL DUE TO INJURY

1081
00:50:23,186 --> 00:50:24,604
I prayed my knees gave out.

1082
00:50:24,688 --> 00:50:26,773
I wished my knees were totally injured.

1083
00:50:26,857 --> 00:50:28,316
I was ready to quit the show.

1084
00:50:28,900 --> 00:50:29,943
Please be injured badly.

1085
00:50:30,026 --> 00:50:33,613
But I went and took an X-ray,
and they said I was fine.

1086
00:50:33,697 --> 00:50:35,615
So I said, "Please check again."

1087
00:50:36,158 --> 00:50:37,117
I'm serious.

1088
00:50:37,200 --> 00:50:38,577
"Doctor, please."

1089
00:50:38,660 --> 00:50:40,537
"Then, take an MRI."

1090
00:50:41,329 --> 00:50:43,749
I couldn't take it there,
so I went to another hospital.

1091
00:50:43,832 --> 00:50:44,750
I took an MRI.

1092
00:50:44,833 --> 00:50:45,667
Nothing was wrong.

1093
00:50:46,209 --> 00:50:47,043
Really?

1094
00:50:47,794 --> 00:50:49,671
But I heard you had a ligament issue.

1095
00:50:50,172 --> 00:50:51,548
I think the doctor did their best

1096
00:50:51,631 --> 00:50:53,467
to find a problem.

1097
00:50:54,301 --> 00:50:55,594
I'm sure you have it too.

1098
00:50:57,220 --> 00:50:58,597
I'm sure you have the same issue.

1099
00:50:58,680 --> 00:51:00,223
-Chae-min too.
-Chae-min's wrist.

1100
00:51:00,307 --> 00:51:01,767
I heard Chae-min fell?

1101
00:51:01,850 --> 00:51:03,477
WEARING A WRIST BRACE DUE TO INJURY

1102
00:51:03,560 --> 00:51:05,979
It's okay.
It's just inflammation and whatnot.

1103
00:51:06,062 --> 00:51:09,316
If it hurts tomorrow,
I'm afraid I won't be able to climb.

1104
00:51:10,025 --> 00:51:10,859
Does it hurt now?

1105
00:51:10,942 --> 00:51:12,194
-Yes, it still hurts.
-What?

1106
00:51:12,277 --> 00:51:14,279
-I still have the brace on.
-So you can't go.

1107
00:51:14,362 --> 00:51:15,822
You can't hold the poles, right?

1108
00:51:15,906 --> 00:51:17,616
I don't think I can.

1109
00:51:17,699 --> 00:51:21,328
I was so depressed last night.

1110
00:51:22,287 --> 00:51:24,581
Why? You're on top
of the Melon music chart.

1111
00:51:25,916 --> 00:51:27,167
FOR THE FIRST TIME IN 14 YEARS,

1112
00:51:27,250 --> 00:51:28,460
HE'S NUMBER ONE ON MELON TOO

1113
00:51:28,543 --> 00:51:29,961
<i>You shouldn't be feeling down.</i>

1114
00:51:30,045 --> 00:51:32,339
Saying this while I'm sitting
in between these two

1115
00:51:32,422 --> 00:51:34,174
is a bit embarrassing,

1116
00:51:34,257 --> 00:51:35,634
but let me stay there for a while.

1117
00:51:36,343 --> 00:51:37,177
Just for a bit.

1118
00:51:37,260 --> 00:51:39,721
I know that as soon as you release
your albums,

1119
00:51:39,805 --> 00:51:40,764
things will change.

1120
00:51:40,847 --> 00:51:42,516
But let me stay there for a moment.

1121
00:51:42,599 --> 00:51:44,392
How's the air up there?

1122
00:51:44,476 --> 00:51:46,019
I didn't know before either.

1123
00:51:46,102 --> 00:51:46,937
At the top…

1124
00:51:47,437 --> 00:51:48,271
You knew, right?

1125
00:51:48,355 --> 00:51:50,315
You two knew about this feeling, right?

1126
00:51:51,233 --> 00:51:52,526
During my music career,

1127
00:51:52,609 --> 00:51:54,861
I didn't know
this kind of level in the air existed.

1128
00:51:56,071 --> 00:51:57,197
THE TOP TASTES SWEET

1129
00:51:57,280 --> 00:51:58,573
You're still number one.

1130
00:51:58,657 --> 00:51:59,491
It felt really good.

1131
00:52:00,075 --> 00:52:02,494
It's like the Huiungak Shelter.

1132
00:52:02,577 --> 00:52:03,411
Geez, stop it.

1133
00:52:03,495 --> 00:52:05,205
No joke. I literally got goosebumps.

1134
00:52:05,288 --> 00:52:06,832
Huiungak…

1135
00:52:06,915 --> 00:52:09,000
I erased its existence from my head.

1136
00:52:09,084 --> 00:52:09,960
Huiungak…

1137
00:52:10,710 --> 00:52:12,087
How have you all been?

1138
00:52:12,170 --> 00:52:15,715
It's been over ten days
since the last shoot.

1139
00:52:16,675 --> 00:52:18,176
Other commitments felt much easier.

1140
00:52:19,553 --> 00:52:21,179
Chae-min was abroad too.

1141
00:52:21,680 --> 00:52:22,973
HE WENT TO A PARIS FASHION SHOW

1142
00:52:23,056 --> 00:52:25,600
Chae-min was at the fashion show.

1143
00:52:25,684 --> 00:52:26,685
A different world.

1144
00:52:26,768 --> 00:52:28,061
You're so cool, Chae-min.

1145
00:52:28,812 --> 00:52:29,646
Not at all.

1146
00:52:29,729 --> 00:52:31,731
Then, did you walk on a runaway?

1147
00:52:31,815 --> 00:52:32,649
Runaway?

1148
00:52:32,732 --> 00:52:34,484
Runway, not runaway.

1149
00:52:34,568 --> 00:52:36,236
BECOMES A RUNAWAY FROM THE FASHION SHOW

1150
00:52:36,319 --> 00:52:37,821
He shouldn't run away.

1151
00:52:37,904 --> 00:52:38,905
What was it?

1152
00:52:38,989 --> 00:52:40,323
Runaway and runway are the same.

1153
00:52:40,407 --> 00:52:41,241
What was it?

1154
00:52:41,324 --> 00:52:43,493
Hold on, what was it called?

1155
00:52:43,994 --> 00:52:45,078
-Runway.
-Runway.

1156
00:52:45,161 --> 00:52:47,038
-Oh, runway.
-Runaway!

1157
00:52:47,122 --> 00:52:49,040
Runaway or runway. Same difference.

1158
00:52:49,124 --> 00:52:51,042
-They're all the same.
-As long as they get it.

1159
00:52:51,126 --> 00:52:53,587
Also, the person who used to work
at your agency

1160
00:52:53,670 --> 00:52:54,838
moved to my agency.

1161
00:52:54,921 --> 00:52:56,423
-There's one person who joined.
-Okay.

1162
00:52:56,506 --> 00:52:58,758
Do you go around saying this is fun?

1163
00:53:00,427 --> 00:53:02,596
Who on earth… What's their name?

1164
00:53:02,679 --> 00:53:03,930
You're going to get it.

1165
00:53:05,557 --> 00:53:07,267
Anyway, you came back from hiking

1166
00:53:07,809 --> 00:53:09,352
and told people at THEBLACKLABEL,

1167
00:53:09,436 --> 00:53:11,146
"It was fun."

1168
00:53:11,646 --> 00:53:12,898
You said that.

1169
00:53:14,065 --> 00:53:14,900
"What?"

1170
00:53:15,400 --> 00:53:16,443
"What's wrong with him?"

1171
00:53:16,526 --> 00:53:18,278
"Why would he go around saying that?"

1172
00:53:18,361 --> 00:53:21,156
Because of that,
I was a bit upset with you.

1173
00:53:22,115 --> 00:53:22,949
Hear me out.

1174
00:53:23,033 --> 00:53:28,330
After it was over, I got in the car
and barely spoke a word with my manager.

1175
00:53:28,413 --> 00:53:29,706
-What did you say?
-"Thank you."

1176
00:53:30,206 --> 00:53:32,208
"Thank you for coming all the way here."

1177
00:53:32,292 --> 00:53:33,168
I was so exhausted.

1178
00:53:33,251 --> 00:53:36,588
I didn't even say
anything like, "It was fun."

1179
00:53:37,088 --> 00:53:38,506
-It was distorted.
-Yes, it was.

1180
00:53:38,590 --> 00:53:39,799
-So that's what happened.
-Yes.

1181
00:53:39,883 --> 00:53:41,092
Let us all watch out.

1182
00:53:41,176 --> 00:53:42,010
Okay.

1183
00:53:42,093 --> 00:53:44,346
Don't say stuff like, "It was fun,"
"I enjoyed it,"

1184
00:53:44,429 --> 00:53:46,640
or "It was rewarding."

1185
00:53:47,474 --> 00:53:48,808
You don't have to worry about me.

1186
00:53:48,892 --> 00:53:51,603
I keep telling those around me
that I've been scammed.

1187
00:53:52,312 --> 00:53:53,688
I've said that a lot too.

1188
00:53:54,189 --> 00:53:56,566
Dowoon, in the group chat…

1189
00:53:56,650 --> 00:53:58,318
-Yes?
-Why do you type in a dialect?

1190
00:53:58,818 --> 00:54:00,654
I've seen people speak in a dialect,

1191
00:54:00,737 --> 00:54:02,781
but I've never seen anyone
text in a dialect too.

1192
00:54:02,864 --> 00:54:04,699
But Busan people do that often.

1193
00:54:04,783 --> 00:54:06,534
They type, "Go ahead" in a dialect.

1194
00:54:07,118 --> 00:54:08,370
DOWOON
YEAH, GET WELL SOON

1195
00:54:08,453 --> 00:54:09,454
HOW ARE YOUR LEGS?

1196
00:54:09,537 --> 00:54:11,665
ENJOY THE FOOD
CAN YOU OPEN THE DOOR?

1197
00:54:11,748 --> 00:54:13,416
I HEAR THEY SELL RAMYEON ON THE SUMMIT

1198
00:54:13,500 --> 00:54:15,335
A COLLECTION OF TEXTS
FROM A GYEONGSANG PERSON

1199
00:54:15,418 --> 00:54:18,463
"Jeju Island '<i>naena</i>,'
I hear they sell <i>ramyeon </i>on the summit."

1200
00:54:18,546 --> 00:54:19,881
What's "<i>naena</i>"?

1201
00:54:20,590 --> 00:54:22,634
Jeju Island <i>naena…</i>

1202
00:54:22,717 --> 00:54:23,969
How do I explain this?

1203
00:54:24,052 --> 00:54:25,637
How do I explain "<i>naena</i>"?

1204
00:54:25,720 --> 00:54:27,472
-You wrote it.
-Jeju Island <i>naena?</i>

1205
00:54:28,306 --> 00:54:29,265
<i>Naena.</i>

1206
00:54:29,349 --> 00:54:30,600
There must be a meaning to it.

1207
00:54:30,684 --> 00:54:31,518
<i>Naena</i> Jeju Island…

1208
00:54:31,601 --> 00:54:34,646
"Well, on Jeju Island,
I heard they sell <i>ramyeon</i> on the summit."

1209
00:54:34,729 --> 00:54:36,898
It's "well." Like, "Well, on Jeju Island…"

1210
00:54:36,982 --> 00:54:39,526
Give us another example
of how you use <i>naena.</i>

1211
00:54:39,609 --> 00:54:40,485
An example.

1212
00:54:40,568 --> 00:54:41,403
The everyday usage.

1213
00:54:41,486 --> 00:54:42,320
When do you use it?

1214
00:54:42,404 --> 00:54:44,114
<i>Naena</i>, I can just use it like this.

1215
00:54:44,197 --> 00:54:45,949
What?

1216
00:54:46,032 --> 00:54:47,283
DID ANYONE UNDERSTAND THAT?

1217
00:54:47,367 --> 00:54:48,827
I don't think people use it often.

1218
00:54:48,910 --> 00:54:50,370
Not often? That's not true.

1219
00:54:50,453 --> 00:54:52,163
Is it language only you use?

1220
00:54:52,247 --> 00:54:53,665
No, a lot of people use <i>naena.</i>

1221
00:54:53,748 --> 00:54:55,250
Chae-min, that was great timing.

1222
00:54:55,333 --> 00:54:56,167
"What?"

1223
00:54:56,751 --> 00:54:58,169
NOBODY UNDERSTOOD NAENA

1224
00:54:58,253 --> 00:54:59,421
That was so good.

1225
00:55:00,213 --> 00:55:01,840
It means "likewise."

1226
00:55:01,923 --> 00:55:03,800
NAENA
A DIALECT WORD FOR "LIKEWISE" OR "ANYWAY"

1227
00:55:03,883 --> 00:55:05,343
-It's something like that.
-"Anyway."

1228
00:55:05,427 --> 00:55:06,720
Right. Wait, "anyway"?

1229
00:55:07,637 --> 00:55:08,680
Where are you from?

1230
00:55:08,763 --> 00:55:11,099
My accent's a mix of Changwon and Busan.

1231
00:55:12,475 --> 00:55:13,309
This is what it is.

1232
00:55:13,393 --> 00:55:16,730
<i>Naena</i> is like, "They're all the same."

1233
00:55:17,647 --> 00:55:19,190
-"They're all the same."
-Yes.

1234
00:55:19,274 --> 00:55:20,984
-"Likewise."
-<i>Naena</i> no difference.

1235
00:55:21,067 --> 00:55:22,861
-"Either way."
-Yes, something like that.

1236
00:55:22,944 --> 00:55:24,320
"<i>Naena</i> no difference."

1237
00:55:25,071 --> 00:55:27,198
I'm sorry, but in "<i>Naena</i> no difference,"

1238
00:55:27,282 --> 00:55:28,742
which part of that is Korean?

1239
00:55:29,325 --> 00:55:30,201
The "ji" part.

1240
00:55:30,702 --> 00:55:32,162
The "ji" at the end was Korean.

1241
00:55:32,245 --> 00:55:33,621
Something "ji."

1242
00:55:33,705 --> 00:55:35,040
"<i>Ddoiddoi</i>" isn't Korean?

1243
00:55:35,123 --> 00:55:35,957
I don't know.

1244
00:55:36,750 --> 00:55:37,751
Is it a slang?

1245
00:55:37,834 --> 00:55:38,668
"Slang"!

1246
00:55:39,586 --> 00:55:41,046
THE LINGUIST WHO GOES BEYOND BORDERS

1247
00:55:41,129 --> 00:55:42,213
It's slang?

1248
00:55:42,297 --> 00:55:43,798
Let's give a few dialect questions.

1249
00:55:44,632 --> 00:55:45,467
Okay.

1250
00:55:45,550 --> 00:55:46,384
DIALECT QUIZ STARTS

1251
00:55:46,468 --> 00:55:48,720
We're slowly getting quizzes now.

1252
00:55:48,803 --> 00:55:49,846
Here come the quizzes.

1253
00:55:49,929 --> 00:55:51,056
ANYTHING BUT HIKING WELCOMED

1254
00:55:51,139 --> 00:55:52,182
It's better to have them.

1255
00:55:52,265 --> 00:55:54,267
But I don't know
the correct intonation either.

1256
00:55:54,350 --> 00:55:57,270
She is from Gyeongsang Province.

1257
00:55:57,353 --> 00:55:58,772
Where are you from, U-jeong?

1258
00:55:58,855 --> 00:56:00,023
-Jinju.
-Jinju.

1259
00:56:00,106 --> 00:56:00,982
Jinju?

1260
00:56:01,066 --> 00:56:02,484
Jinju is a bit on the outskirts.

1261
00:56:03,860 --> 00:56:05,361
Hey, are you nitpicking?

1262
00:56:06,237 --> 00:56:07,822
Jinju has 400,000 citizens!

1263
00:56:08,323 --> 00:56:09,157
I'm sorry.

1264
00:56:09,240 --> 00:56:10,909
People from Jinju will turn on you.

1265
00:56:10,992 --> 00:56:12,202
JINJU PEOPLE, COVER YOUR EARS

1266
00:56:12,285 --> 00:56:13,787
The western part of South Gyeongsang…

1267
00:56:13,870 --> 00:56:15,205
Jinju, "The City of Education."

1268
00:56:15,288 --> 00:56:16,748
Okay. I wonder if Dowoon knows this.

1269
00:56:16,831 --> 00:56:17,791
GYEONGSANG DIALECT QUIZ

1270
00:56:17,874 --> 00:56:19,709
I'll say them without the intonation.

1271
00:56:19,793 --> 00:56:21,628
You're so "<i>kkaelbatda</i>."

1272
00:56:21,711 --> 00:56:22,754
-Sorry?
-Sorry?

1273
00:56:22,837 --> 00:56:24,297
You're so "<i>kkaelbatda</i>."

1274
00:56:24,380 --> 00:56:27,467
See? Jinju is a bit on the outskirts.

1275
00:56:28,635 --> 00:56:29,719
"You're so foolish."

1276
00:56:30,220 --> 00:56:31,888
-Wrong.
-Wrong.

1277
00:56:31,971 --> 00:56:32,806
<i>Kkaelbatda.</i>

1278
00:56:32,889 --> 00:56:35,558
I like everything about Chae-min,
but he's <i>kkaelbatda.</i>

1279
00:56:36,810 --> 00:56:37,852
"Dumb."

1280
00:56:40,063 --> 00:56:40,897
INSULTING HIMSELF

1281
00:56:40,980 --> 00:56:42,774
-He called himself that.
-He dissed himself.

1282
00:56:42,857 --> 00:56:43,691
He dissed himself.

1283
00:56:43,775 --> 00:56:45,443
Out of the four here,

1284
00:56:45,527 --> 00:56:48,321
Car, the garden is the most <i>kkaelbatda.</i>

1285
00:56:49,489 --> 00:56:50,698
-"Talkative."
-"Talkative"?

1286
00:56:50,782 --> 00:56:51,658
"Grumpy."

1287
00:56:52,992 --> 00:56:53,827
"Ugly"?

1288
00:56:54,452 --> 00:56:55,495
Seriously…

1289
00:56:55,578 --> 00:56:56,663
<i>-Kkaelbatda?</i>
<i>-Kkaelbatda?</i>

1290
00:56:56,746 --> 00:56:57,622
WHAT'S "KKAELBATDA"?

1291
00:56:57,705 --> 00:56:58,665
"Make you angry"?

1292
00:56:58,748 --> 00:56:59,582
It's <i>kkaelbatda.</i>

1293
00:56:59,666 --> 00:57:01,376
The tone sounds like he's cursing.

1294
00:57:01,459 --> 00:57:03,211
Exactly. It doesn't sound nice.

1295
00:57:03,962 --> 00:57:05,839
"Why is he so <i>kkaelbatda</i>?"

1296
00:57:07,132 --> 00:57:08,299
Have you heard of it before?

1297
00:57:08,383 --> 00:57:10,552
-I've heard of "<i>kkolbatda</i>."
-I've heard of that too.

1298
00:57:10,635 --> 00:57:11,928
Who is the most <i>kkaelbatda</i> here?

1299
00:57:12,011 --> 00:57:13,847
I really think it's Car, the garden.

1300
00:57:13,930 --> 00:57:15,431
DOWOON AND TARZZAN DON'T KNOW EITHER

1301
00:57:15,515 --> 00:57:16,683
"Grumpy"?

1302
00:57:16,766 --> 00:57:19,060
Now that he actually gave us a quiz,
we can't answer.

1303
00:57:19,144 --> 00:57:20,019
It's difficult.

1304
00:57:20,103 --> 00:57:21,438
"Why is it so <i>kkaelbatda</i>?"

1305
00:57:21,521 --> 00:57:22,814
-It means "lazy."
-Really?

1306
00:57:22,897 --> 00:57:24,399
But for a word meaning "lazy,"

1307
00:57:24,482 --> 00:57:26,067
it sounds very antagonistic.

1308
00:57:27,527 --> 00:57:29,362
THEY'RE SO BAD,
SO DIFFICULTY IS LOWERED

1309
00:57:29,446 --> 00:57:30,655
It's clearly antagonistic.

1310
00:57:30,738 --> 00:57:32,282
Then, how about this?

1311
00:57:32,365 --> 00:57:33,700
"<i>Neoljjatda</i>."

1312
00:57:33,783 --> 00:57:35,493
I've heard of <i>neoljjatda</i> before.

1313
00:57:35,577 --> 00:57:36,744
THEY KNOW THE WORD

1314
00:57:36,828 --> 00:57:37,662
I know this one.

1315
00:57:37,745 --> 00:57:39,414
Dowoon, give us the native pronunciation.

1316
00:57:39,497 --> 00:57:40,582
Those from Seoul can guess.

1317
00:57:40,665 --> 00:57:43,918
I know this one,
but I've never used it before.

1318
00:57:44,002 --> 00:57:45,044
WHAT?

1319
00:57:45,128 --> 00:57:46,463
So you don't know how to say it?

1320
00:57:46,546 --> 00:57:49,424
I don't remember the meaning,
but I've heard it a lot before.

1321
00:57:49,507 --> 00:57:50,341
WHAT DO YOU MEAN?

1322
00:57:50,425 --> 00:57:51,301
What's with you?

1323
00:57:51,384 --> 00:57:52,218
Hey!

1324
00:57:52,302 --> 00:57:54,345
He's a fake. A fake Gyeongsang person.

1325
00:57:54,429 --> 00:57:55,263
He's a fake!

1326
00:57:55,972 --> 00:57:57,891
He was going for the down-to-earth vibe.

1327
00:57:58,391 --> 00:57:59,934
He was using a fake dialect.

1328
00:58:00,018 --> 00:58:01,561
-"Down-to-earth vibe"!
-"Fake dialect"!

1329
00:58:01,644 --> 00:58:03,396
"Going for the down-to-earth vibe"!

1330
00:58:05,523 --> 00:58:07,150
We need an example sentence.

1331
00:58:07,233 --> 00:58:08,318
Exactly.

1332
00:58:08,401 --> 00:58:10,612
Can you give us
an example sentence using <i>neoljjatda?</i>

1333
00:58:11,196 --> 00:58:12,071
<i>"Neoljja</i> me here."

1334
00:58:12,155 --> 00:58:13,531
"Leave me alone."

1335
00:58:13,615 --> 00:58:14,532
Wrong.

1336
00:58:15,742 --> 00:58:19,120
-"Drop me off here."
-Right.

1337
00:58:19,204 --> 00:58:20,330
Correct.

1338
00:58:20,413 --> 00:58:21,789
He's right.

1339
00:58:21,873 --> 00:58:22,707
CHAE-MIN IS CORRECT

1340
00:58:22,790 --> 00:58:23,666
Drop someone off.

1341
00:58:23,750 --> 00:58:25,418
They say <i>neoljja</i>. That's weird.

1342
00:58:26,377 --> 00:58:28,129
Normally, they say "drop off."

1343
00:58:28,213 --> 00:58:30,131
"Drop off" or "give a lift."

1344
00:58:30,215 --> 00:58:31,299
I'm disappointed, Dowoon.

1345
00:58:31,382 --> 00:58:32,383
You were a fake.

1346
00:58:32,467 --> 00:58:34,552
He could actually be a true Seoulite.

1347
00:58:34,636 --> 00:58:36,012
Totally.

1348
00:58:36,095 --> 00:58:37,972
If that's the case, he's incredible.

1349
00:58:39,265 --> 00:58:40,099
We got here quick.

1350
00:58:40,183 --> 00:58:42,101
SOON ARRIVING
AT GIMPO INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT

1351
00:58:42,185 --> 00:58:44,687
Actually, the real hike
will start tomorrow.

1352
00:58:44,771 --> 00:58:46,189
Today, as hiking club members,

1353
00:58:46,272 --> 00:58:49,192
you'll prepare for it
and build up your teamwork.

1354
00:58:49,275 --> 00:58:50,360
HALLASAN HIKE IS TOMORROW

1355
00:58:50,443 --> 00:58:51,986
Today is for you to get ready.

1356
00:58:52,070 --> 00:58:55,532
You'll be taking it easy today.
Right, President Tar?

1357
00:58:55,615 --> 00:58:57,742
President Tar,
could you brief us on the schedule?

1358
00:58:58,785 --> 00:59:00,245
I need to see the schedule.

1359
00:59:00,787 --> 00:59:01,704
I don't remember.

1360
00:59:01,788 --> 00:59:02,830
3 DAYS AGO

1361
00:59:02,914 --> 00:59:03,748
Hello.

1362
00:59:05,291 --> 00:59:08,127
You planned a lot when you were in LA.

1363
00:59:10,505 --> 00:59:12,215
A LONG TEXT MESSAGE FROM LA

1364
00:59:12,298 --> 00:59:13,550
3 DAYS AND 2 NIGHTS IN JEJU

1365
00:59:13,633 --> 00:59:15,510
What was the criteria for the plan?

1366
00:59:15,593 --> 00:59:17,136
Well, the criteria was,

1367
00:59:17,637 --> 00:59:21,683
"How can we make use
of the little time we have on Jeju Island

1368
00:59:21,766 --> 00:59:24,477
to go and do some fun things?"

1369
00:59:24,561 --> 00:59:25,395
Okay, then.

1370
00:59:25,478 --> 00:59:27,855
PRESIDENT TAR
AMBITIOUSLY PREPARED THEIR JEJU TRIP

1371
00:59:28,940 --> 00:59:30,400
Yes, we'll depart,

1372
00:59:31,025 --> 00:59:33,486
and arrive at Jeju Airport
between 11:00 a.m. and 1:00 p.m.

1373
00:59:33,570 --> 00:59:35,363
PICK UP RENTAL CAR
AT 1:00 P.M. AT AIRPORT

1374
00:59:35,446 --> 00:59:37,198
We'll rent a car.

1375
00:59:37,282 --> 00:59:39,033
-Then, we'll go for lunch.
-Nice.

1376
00:59:39,117 --> 00:59:40,910
Lunch is cold raw abalone soup.

1377
00:59:41,411 --> 00:59:42,495
-Sounds good.
-Sounds good.

1378
00:59:42,579 --> 00:59:43,413
What do we do next?

1379
00:59:43,496 --> 00:59:45,790
And for a physical activity,

1380
00:59:45,873 --> 00:59:47,750
we'll go to Jeju Big Ball Land.

1381
00:59:47,834 --> 00:59:49,377
-Big Ball Land.
-Big Ball Land.

1382
00:59:51,421 --> 00:59:53,881
At least we get to ride a plane.

1383
00:59:53,965 --> 00:59:55,633
STARTING UNDER PRESIDENT TAR'S DIRECTION

1384
00:59:57,010 --> 01:00:03,975
DESCEND CLUB'S FIRST EXPEDITION
TO JEJU ISLAND

1385
01:00:04,058 --> 01:00:04,976
Where's the mountain?

1386
01:00:05,059 --> 01:00:06,936
DESCEND CLUB IS HAPPY
IF THERE'S NO HIKING

1387
01:00:07,020 --> 01:00:08,980
Look how close we've become.

1388
01:00:10,773 --> 01:00:12,025
<i>Tarzzan found this place?</i>

1389
01:00:12,108 --> 01:00:13,401
<i>Good job finding it.</i>

1390
01:00:14,861 --> 01:00:18,406
THEY'LL HAVE A LUXURIOUS TRIP
THANKS TO THEIR FOODIE PRESIDENT

1391
01:00:18,489 --> 01:00:19,699
This is so good.

1392
01:00:21,576 --> 01:00:22,410
Good job finding it.

1393
01:00:22,493 --> 01:00:23,328
THUMBS UP

1394
01:00:23,411 --> 01:00:25,788
I want to feed the sheep too.

1395
01:00:30,001 --> 01:00:31,336
He's actually doing it.

1396
01:00:31,419 --> 01:00:33,463
THE PRESIDENT UNLEASHES HIS PLAYFUL SIDE

1397
01:00:34,297 --> 01:00:35,340
THE OTHERS BECOME WEIRDER

1398
01:00:35,423 --> 01:00:37,091
Hey, what's going on?

1399
01:00:40,219 --> 01:00:41,054
You little punk.

1400
01:00:43,723 --> 01:00:44,807
Whoa!

1401
01:01:45,159 --> 01:01:47,161
Subtitle translation by: Kim Yeeun
